      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solution(s):\n    s_list = list(s)\n    \n    # Handle hours - first digit (index 0)\n    if s_list[0] == '?':\n        # If second digit is '?' or between '0'-'1', we can use '1' for first digit\n        # Otherwise, if second digit is '2'-'9', we must use '0'\n        if s_list[1] == '?' or s_list[1] <= '1':\n            s_list[0] = '1'\n        else:\n            s_list[0] = '0'\n    \n    # Handle hours - second digit (index 1)\n    if s_list[1] == '?':\n        # If first digit is '1', second digit can be at most '1' (for 11)\n        # If first digit is '0', second digit can be at most '9' (for 09)\n        if s_list[0] == '1':\n            s_list[1] = '1'\n        else:\n            s_list[1] = '9'\n    \n    # Handle minutes - first digit (index 3)\n    if s_list[3] == '?':\n        # First digit of minutes can be at most '5'\n        s_list[3] = '5'\n    \n    # Handle minutes - second digit (index 4)\n    if s_list[4] == '?':\n        # Second digit of minutes can be at most '9'\n        s_list[4] = '9'\n    \n    return ''.join(s_list)\n```",
