safe cell. But the non-safe cell itself has degree freedom 1. So we only care about computing reachable count for safe cells.\n\nWe must ensure we count each boundary cell only once per component.\n\nComplexities: H,W up to 1000, so O(H*W) is fine.\n\nLet's implement.\n\nWe'll read grid, create a 2D array safe bool.\nFor each cell, if it's '.' and all neighbors (within grid) are not '#', then safe=True.\n\nThen BFS over safe cells to find components.\nFor each component, we maintain list of cells and a set of boundary cells (non-safe '.' cells adjacent to any cell in component).\n\nAfter BFS, compute component_reachable = len(component_cells) + len(boundary_set).\n\nAssign to each safe cell in component this value.\n\nThen for each '.' cell, if not safe, value=1.\n\nTake max over all '.' cells.\n\nEdge cases: isolated safe cells (component size 1) may have boundary cells.\n\nLet's code.\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    H, W = int(data[0]), int(data[1])\n    grid = data[2:]\n    \n    safe = [[False] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    \n    # compute safe cells\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                # check four neighbors\n                ok = True\n                for di, dj in [(0,1),(0,-1),(1,0),(-1,0)]:\n                    ni, nj = i + di, j + dj\n                    if 0 <= ni < H and 0 <= nj < W:\n                        if grid[ni][nj] == '#':\n                            ok = False\n                            break\n                if ok:\n                    safe[i][j] = True\n    \n    visited = [[False] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    component_id = [[-1] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    component_info = []  # list of (size, boundary_set)\n    \n    from collections import deque\n    \n    # BFS over safe cells to find components\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if safe[i][j] and not visited[i][j]:\n                q = deque()\n                q.append((i, j))\n                visited[i][j] = True\n                cells = []\n                boundary = set()\n                while q:\n                    ci, cj = q.popleft()\n                    cells.append((ci, cj))\n                    # check neighbors for safe cells to expand component\n                    for di, dj in [(0,1),(0,-1),(1,0),(-1,0)]:\n                        ni, nj = ci + di, cj + dj\n                        if 0 <= ni < H and 0 <= nj < W:\n                            if safe[ni][nj] and not visited[ni][nj]:\n                                visited[ni][nj] = True\n                                q.append((ni, nj))\n                            elif grid[ni][nj] == '.' and not safe[ni][nj]:\n                                boundary.add((ni, nj))\n                # store component info\n                comp_id = len(component_info)\n                for (ci, cj) in cells:\n                    component_id[ci][cj] = comp_id\n                component_info.append((len(cells), boundary))\n    \n    # compute reachable count for each safe cell\n    reachable = [[0] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                if safe[i][j]:\n                    comp_id = component_id[i][j]\n                    size, boundary = component_info[comp_id]\n                    reachable[i][j] = size + len(boundary)\n                else:\n                    reachable[i][j] = 1\n    \n    # find maximum\n    ans = 0\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                ans = max(ans, reachable[i][j])\n    \n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
