      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\n\ndef solve(s: str) -> str:\n    # Count the frequency of each character in the string\n    freq = Counter(s)\n    max_freq = max(freq.values())\n    \n    # The number of operations before the last one is max_freq - 1\n    # We build the string by keeping only characters whose occurrence index\n    # in the original string is greater than max_freq - 1\n    result = []\n    occurrence_count = defaultdict(int)\n    threshold = max_freq - 1\n    \n    for char in s:\n        occurrence_count[char] += 1\n        if occurrence_count[char] > threshold:\n            result.append(char)\n    \n    return ''.join(result)\n```",
