      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef makeSmallestPalindrome(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Makes the given string a palindrome with minimum operations,\n    returning the lexicographically smallest palindrome possible.\n    \n    Args:\n        s (str): Input string consisting of lowercase English letters\n        \n    Returns:\n        str: The lexicographically smallest palindrome that can be made\n             with minimum operations\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert string to list for easier manipulation\n    chars = list(s)\n    n = len(s)\n    \n    # Process pairs from both ends moving inward\n    for i in range(n // 2):\n        left_char = chars[i]\n        right_char = chars[n - 1 - i]\n        \n        # If characters don't match, replace with lexicographically smaller one\n        if left_char != right_char:\n            # Choose the smaller character lexicographically\n            smaller_char = min(left_char, right_char)\n            chars[i] = smaller_char\n            chars[n - 1 - i] = smaller_char\n    \n    # Convert back to string and return\n    return ''.join(chars)\n```",
