te `comp[r]`, we need a way to get root of a player.\n\nBut we can maintain an array `current_root[i]`: the current root of the component that contains player i.\n\nInitially, `current_root[i] = i`.\n\nWhen we merge two components with roots `rp` and `rq`, we:\n- pick new root (we can keep one as root)\n- merge smaller into larger\n- update `current_root[x] = new_root` for all x in smaller component\n\nWe’ll maintain:\n- `size[r]`\n- `members[r]`\n- `current_root[i]` for each player i\n\nBut `current_root[i]` will be updated only when i is in the smaller component during merge.\n\nWe do small-to-large: the smaller component is merged into the larger one.\n\nLet’s do:\n\n```python\nimport sys\ninput = sys.stdin.read\n\nMOD = 998244353\n\ndef modinv(a):\n    return pow(a, MOD-2, MOD)\n\ndef main():\n    data = input().split()\n    N = int(data[0])\n    matches = []\n    idx = 1\n    for i in range(N-1):\n        p = int(data[idx]); q = int(data[idx+1]); idx += 2\n        matches.append((p, q))\n    \n    # Initialize\n    ans = [0] * (N+1)  # 1-indexed: ans[1..N]\n    current_root = [i for i in range(N+1)]  # current_root[i] = root of component containing i\n    size = [1] * (N+1)   # size[r] = size of component with root r\n    members = [[] for _ in range(N+1)]\n    for i in range(1, N+1):\n        members[i] = [i]\n\n    # Process each match\n    for p, q in matches:\n        rp = current_root[p]\n        rq = current_root[q]\n        if rp == rq:\n            continue  # should not happen per constraints\n        a = size[rp]\n        b = size[rq]\n        total = a + b\n        # Probability that first team (p's team) wins\n        prob_p_win = (a * modinv(total)) % MOD\n        # Probability that second team (q's team) wins\n        prob_q_win = (b * modinv(total)) % MOD\n\n        # Add contributions to all players in both teams\n        for player in members[rp]:\n            ans[player] = (ans[player] + prob_p_win) % MOD\n        for player in members[rq]:\n            ans[player] = (ans[player] + prob_q_win) % MOD\n\n        # Merge smaller component into larger one\n        if size[rp] < size[rq]:\n            # Merge rp into rq\n            new_root = rq\n            # Update all members of rp\n            for player in members[rp]:\n                current_root[player] = new_root\n            members[rq].extend(members[rp])\n            size[rq] += size[rp]\n            # Clear rp\n            members[rp] = []\n        else:\n            # Merge rq into rp\n            new_root = rp\n            for player in members[rq]:\n                current_root[player] = new_root\n            members[rp].extend(members[rq])\n            size[rp] += size[rq]\n            members[rq] = []\n\n    # Output\n    print(' '.join(str(ans[i]) for i in range(1, N+1)))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```\n\nBut note: the **first team is the one with p_i**, and the **second team is the one with q_i** — the problem says:\n> The team with player p_i goes first, and the team with player q_i goes second.\n\nSo it’s not symmetric: the first team wins with probability `a/(a+b)`, and that contributes to **all players in the first team**.\n\nIn our code, `p` is first, `q` is second.\n\nSo we must use:\n- `rp` = component of `p` → first team\n- `rq` = component of `q` → second team\n\nThen:\n- add `a/(a+b)` to all in `rp`\n- add `b/(a+b)` to all in `rq`\n\nYes, that’s what we did.\n\nAlso, we are merging into a new component — correct.\n\nBut small-to-large ensures that each player is moved at most O(log N) times, and total number of operations is O(N log N), which is acceptable for N ≤ 2e5.\n\nLet’s test with sample input:\n\n```\nN=5\nMatches:\n1 2\n4 3\n5 3  -> here, at time of match, 3 is in team with 4? So q_i=3 → team with 3 is second\n1 4\n```\n\nWe process in order.\n\nMatch 1: p=1, q=2\n- rp = 1, size=1; rq=2, size=1\n- prob_p_win = 1 * inv(2) = (1 * 499122177) % MOD = 499122177\n- prob_q_win = same\n- Add 499122177 to player 