      "generated_answer": "We can solve this by generating all possible spanning trees, computing their total weight modulo \\(K\\), and taking the minimum.  \nSince \\(N \\leq 8\\), the number of spanning trees is at most \\(8^{8-2} = 8^6 = 262144\\) by Cayley’s formula, which is manageable.  \n\nWe’ll use recursion to try all subsets of edges of size \\(N-1\\) that form a spanning tree.\n\nHere’s the Python implementation:\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve() -> None:\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    it = iter(input_data)\n    N = int(next(it))\n    M = int(next(it))\n    K = int(next(it))\n\n    edges = []\n    for _ in range(M):\n        u = int(next(it)) - 1\n        v = int(next(it)) - 1\n        w = int(next(it))\n        edges.append((u, v, w))\n\n    # Union-Find for connectivity check\n    parent = list(range(N))\n    rank = [0] * N\n\n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n\n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\n            parent[rx] = ry\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n        else:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n\n    # Try all combinations of N-1 edges\n    from itertools import combinations\n\n    min_cost = K  # Start with max possible mod K, since cost < K\n\n    for combo in combinations(range(M), N - 1):\n        # Reset Union-Find\n        for i in range(N):\n            parent[i] = i\n            rank[i] = 0\n\n        total = 0\n        edges_used = 0\n        for idx in combo:\n            u, v, w = edges[idx]\n            if union(u, v):\n                total = (total + w) % K\n                edges_used += 1\n            else:\n                break  # This combo has a cycle, invalid for spanning tree\n        if edges_used == N - 1:\n            # All vertices connected\n            min_cost = min(min_cost, total)\n\n    print(min_cost)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
