      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom collections import deque\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input\n    H, W = map(int, input().split())\n    grid = []\n    for _ in range(H):\n        grid.append(input().strip())\n    \n    N = int(input())\n    medicines = {}\n    for _ in range(N):\n        r, c, e = map(int, input().split())\n        # Convert to 0-indexed\n        medicines[(r-1, c-1)] = e\n    \n    # Find start and goal\n    start = None\n    goal = None\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == 'S':\n                start = (i, j)\n            elif grid[i][j] == 'T':\n                goal = (i, j)\n    \n    # BFS with state (row, col, energy)\n    # We need to track visited states as (row, col, energy)\n    # But we can optimize by noting that if we've reached (row, col) with energy >= some value,\n    # we don't need to consider lower energies\n    max_energy = H * W  # Maximum possible energy needed\n    visited = {}\n    \n    # visited[(r, c)] will store the maximum energy we've had at (r, c)\n    queue = deque()\n    # Start with 0 energy\n    queue.append((start[0], start[1], 0))\n    visited[(start[0], start[1])] = 0\n    \n    # Directions: up, down, left, right\n    directions = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n    \n    while queue:\n        r, c, energy = queue.popleft()\n        \n        # If current energy is less than what we've had here before, skip\n        if (r, c) in visited and energy < visited[(r, c)]:\n            continue\n            \n        # Check if we reached the goal\n        if (r, c) == goal:\n            print(\"Yes\")\n            return\n            \n        # Use medicine if available at current cell\n        if (r, c) in medicines:\n            new_energy = medicines[(r, c)]\n            if (r, c) not in visited or new_energy > visited[(r, c)]:\n                visited[(r, c)] = new_energy\n                queue.append((r, c, new_energy))\n                continue  # Revisit this cell with new energy\n        \n        # Try to move to adjacent cells\n        if energy > 0:  # Only move if we have energy\n            for dr, dc in directions:\n                nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n                if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W and grid[nr][nc] != '#' and energy > 0:\n                    new_energy = energy - 1\n                    # If we haven't visited this cell or we can reach it with higher energy\n                    if (nr, nc) not in visited or new_energy > visited[(nr, nc)]:\n                        visited[(nr, nc)] = new_energy\n                        queue.append((nr, nc, new_energy))\n    \n    print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
