      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    H, W, N = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    # Initialize grid (0 = white, 1 = black)\n    grid = [[0 for _ in range(W)] for _ in range(H)]\n    \n    # Takahashi's position and direction\n    row, col = 0, 0  # (1,1) in 1-indexed is (0,0) in 0-indexed\n    # Directions: 0 = up, 1 = right, 2 = down, 3 = left\n    direction = 0\n    \n    # Direction vectors: up, right, down, left\n    dr = [-1, 0, 1, 0]\n    dc = [0, 1, 0, -1]\n    \n    for _ in range(N):\n        # Check current cell color\n        if grid[row][col] == 0:  # white\n            # Repaint black\n            grid[row][col] = 1\n            # Rotate 90 degrees clockwise (direction + 1) % 4\n            direction = (direction + 1) % 4\n        else:  # black\n            # Repaint white\n            grid[row][col] = 0\n            # Rotate 90 degrees counterclockwise (direction - 1) % 4\n            direction = (direction - 1) % 4\n        \n        # Move forward one cell in the direction faced\n        row = (row + dr[direction]) % H\n        col = (col + dc[direction]) % W\n    \n    # Output the grid\n    for i in range(H):\n        line = \"\"\n        for j in range(W):\n            line += \"#\" if grid[i][j] == 1 else \".\"\n        print(line)\n\nsolve()\n```",
