    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3.5-9b",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef productMatrix(grid):\n    MOD = 12345\n    n = len(grid)\n    m = len(grid[0])\n    total = n * m\n    \n    # Flatten the grid and apply modulo to each element immediately\n    # to keep numbers small during calculations\n    flattened = [val % MOD for row in grid for val in row]\n    \n    # Compute prefix products modulo MOD\n    # prefix[i] will store the product of all elements before index i\n    # i.e., flattened[0] * ... * flattened[i-1]\n    prefix = [1] * total\n    for i in range(1, total):\n        prefix[i] = (prefix[i-1] * flattened[i-1]) % MOD\n        \n    # Compute suffix products modulo MOD\n    # suffix[i] will store the product of all elements after index i\n    # i.e., flattened[i+1] * ... * flattened[total-1]\n    suffix = [1] * total\n    for i in range(total - 2, -1, -1):\n        suffix[i] = (suffix[i+1] * flattened[i+1]) % MOD\n        \n    # Construct the result matrix\n    result = []\n    current_row = []\n    \n    for i in range(total):\n        # The product of all elements excluding the element at index i\n        # is simply prefix[i] * suffix[i]\n        val = (prefix[i] * suffix[i]) % MOD\n        current_row.append(val)\n        \n        # If the current row is complete (every m-th element), move to the next row\n        if (i + 1) % m == 0:\n            result.append(current_row)\n            current_row = []\n            \n    return result\n```",
