      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input from stdin\n    s = sys.stdin.read().strip()\n    \n    # If the string is empty (though constraints say 1<=|S|), it's technically Yes based on empty definitions.\n    if not s:\n        print(\"Yes\")\n        return\n\n    # An Extended ABC string S is formed by concatenating an Extended A string (only 'A's),\n    # an Extended B string (only 'B's), and an Extended C string (only 'C's).\n    # This implies that all 'A's must appear, followed by all 'B's, followed by all 'C's.\n    # Therefore, the string must be sorted in non-decreasing order of characters 'A', 'B', 'C'.\n    # Since 'A' < 'B' < 'C' in ASCII, we can check if sorting the string yields the same string.\n    \n    sorted_s = \"\".join(sorted(s))\n    \n    if sorted_s == s:\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
