      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    from collections import deque\n    \n    # Read input\n    lines = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    N, M = map(int, lines[0].split())\n    grid = []\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        grid.append(lines[i])\n    \n    # Starting position (2,2) which is 0-indexed (1,1)\n    start_r, start_c = 1, 1\n    \n    # BFS to find all reachable ice squares\n    visited = [[False] * M for _ in range(N)]\n    queue = deque([(start_r, start_c)])\n    visited[start_r][start_c] = True\n    \n    # Count reachable ice squares\n    count = 1  # Start with the initial position\n    \n    # Directions: up, down, left, right\n    dr = [-1, 1, 0, 0]\n    dc = [0, 0, -1, 1]\n    \n    while queue:\n        r, c = queue.popleft()\n        \n        # Try all four directions\n        for i in range(4):\n            nr, nc = r, c\n            \n            # Keep moving in this direction until hitting rock\n            while True:\n                nr_next = nr + dr[i]\n                nc_next = nc + dc[i]\n                \n                # Check if next position is within bounds and not rock\n                if (0 <= nr_next < N and 0 <= nc_next < M and \n                    grid[nr_next][nc_next] == '.'):\n                    nr, nc = nr_next, nc_next\n                else:\n                    # Hit rock or boundary, stop here\n                    break\n            \n            # Check if we ended up at a new position\n            if not visited[nr][nc]:\n                visited[nr][nc] = True\n                count += 1\n                queue.append((nr, nc))\n    \n    print(count)\n\nsolve()\n```",
