      "generated_answer": "We can think of this as a binary search problem.  \n\nWe need to give each bottle a unique binary pattern across friends, so that based on which friends get sick, we can uniquely identify the spoiled bottle.  \n\nThe minimum friends needed is the smallest integer \\( M \\) such that \\( 2^M \\geq N \\).  \n\nHere’s a Python implementation:  \n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.readline\n    print = sys.stdout.write\n\n    N = int(input().strip())\n    \n    # Minimum friends needed: ceil(log2(N))\n    M = 0\n    while (1 << M) < N:\n        M += 1\n    \n    print(f\"{M}\\n\")\n    sys.stdout.flush()\n    \n    # Prepare queries: friend i gets bottles where bit i is set in bottle number's binary representation\n    queries = [[] for _ in range(M)]\n    for bottle in range(1, N + 1):\n        for bit in range(M):\n            if (bottle >> bit) & 1:\n                queries[bit].append(bottle)\n    \n    # Output each friend's bottles\n    for i in range(M):\n        k = len(queries[i])\n        if k == 0:\n            print(f\"0\\n\")\n        else:\n            print(f\"{k} \" + \" \".join(map(str, queries[i])) + \"\\n\")\n        sys.stdout.flush()\n    \n    # Read response string S\n    S = input().strip()\n    \n    # Decode spoiled bottle from binary pattern\n    spoiled = 0\n    for i in range(M):\n        if S[i] == '1':\n            spoiled |= (1 << i)\n    \n    # If spoiled == 0, it means no bottle matched (impossible with our scheme unless N < 2^M)\n    # But since we numbered bottles from 1 to N, we must adjust:\n    if spoiled == 0:\n        spoiled = N  # Happens only if N is power of two and spoiled is last bottle? Let's check logic.\n    \n    # Actually, we need to map binary back to bottle number carefully:\n    # We sent patterns for bottle j (1-based) as binary of j-1, so decode:\n    spoiled_bottle = 0\n    for i in range(M):\n        if S[i] == '1':\n            spoiled_bottle |= (1 << i)\n    spoiled_bottle += 1\n    \n    # But if spoiled_bottle > N, something's wrong. In our scheme, it shouldn't happen.\n    if spoiled_bottle > N:\n        spoiled_bottle = N\n    \n    print(f\"{spoiled_bottle}\\n\")\n    sys.stdout.flush()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
