      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input at once\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    it = iter(input_data)\n    \n    N = int(next(it))\n    initial_order = [next(it) for _ in range(N)]\n    \n    # Build a dictionary to store the current linked list structure\n    # head tracks the first element in the sequence\n    prev = {val: None for val in initial_order}  # predecessor pointer\n    next = {val: None for val in initial_order}  # successor pointer\n    \n    # Link elements in sequence\n    for i in range(N):\n        val = initial_order[i]\n        if i > 0:\n            prev[val] = initial_order[i - 1]\n        if i < N - 1:\n            next[val] = initial_order[i + 1]\n    \n    # Track the current head (first element in the list)\n    head = initial_order[0]\n    \n    Q = int(next(it))\n    \n    for _ in range(Q):\n        query_type = int(next(it))\n        \n        if query_type == 1:\n            # Insert y immediately after x\n            x = next(it)\n            y = next(it)\n            \n            # Find the position of x\n            curr_prev = prev[x]\n            curr_next = next[x]\n            \n            # Update pointers to insert y after x\n            next[x] = y\n            prev[y] = x\n            next[y] = curr_next\n            if curr_next is not None:\n                prev[curr_next] = y\n            \n            # If x was the first element, update head\n            if curr_prev is None:\n                head = x\n            \n            # Register new node\n            next[y] = curr_next\n            if curr_next is not None:\n                prev[curr_next] = y\n            else:\n                next[y] = y  # y is now the last element\n            if curr_prev is None:\n                head = x\n\n        elif query_type == 2:\n            # Remove x\n            x = next(it)\n            \n            curr_prev = prev[x]\n            curr_next = next[x]\n            \n            # Update predecessor's next\n            if curr_prev is not None:\n                next[curr_prev] = curr_next\n            else:\n                head = curr_next\n            \n            # Update successor's prev\n            if curr_next is not None:\n                prev[curr_next] = curr_prev\n            \n            # Remove from dictionaries (optional, to free memory)\n            del prev[x]\n            del next[x]\n\n    # Traverse from head to reconstruct the sequence\n    result = []\n    current = head\n    visited = set()\n    \n    while current is not None:\n        if current in visited:\n            break  # Prevent infinite loop\n        visited.add(current)\n        result.append(current)\n        current = next[current] if next.get(current) is not None else None\n    \n    print(' '.join(result))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    solve()\n```",
