    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nimport math\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    n, d = map(int, data[0].split())\n    \n    points = []\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        x, y = map(int, data[i].split())\n        points.append((x, y))\n    \n    # Initialize infection status - person 1 (index 0) is infected initially\n    infected = [False] * n\n    infected[0] = True\n    \n    # Use BFS to propagate the infection\n    queue = deque([0])  # Start with person 1 (index 0)\n    \n    while queue:\n        current = queue.popleft()\n        current_x, current_y = points[current]\n        \n        # Check all other people\n        for i in range(n):\n            if infected[i]:  # Already infected\n                continue\n                \n            other_x, other_y = points[i]\n            # Calculate Euclidean distance\n            distance = math.sqrt((current_x - other_x) ** 2 + (current_y - other_y) ** 2)\n            \n            # If within distance D, infect this person\n            if distance <= d:\n                infected[i] = True\n                queue.append(i)\n    \n    # Output results\n    for i in range(n):\n        print(\"Yes\" if infected[i] else \"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
