    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minProcessingTime(processorTime, tasks):\n    # Sort processorTime in ascending order\n    processorTime.sort()\n    \n    # Sort tasks in descending order to assign longest tasks first\n    tasks.sort(reverse=True)\n    \n    max_completion_time = 0\n    \n    # Each processor handles 4 tasks\n    for i in range(len(processorTime)):\n        # Get the 4 tasks assigned to processor i\n        # Tasks are assigned in groups of 4 from the sorted list\n        processor_start_time = processorTime[i]\n        \n        # The completion time for this processor is the start time\n        # plus the longest task among its 4 assigned tasks\n        # Since tasks are sorted in descending order, the first task\n        # in each group of 4 will be the longest\n        task_group_start = i * 4\n        longest_task_time = tasks[task_group_start]\n        \n        completion_time = processor_start_time + longest_task_time\n        max_completion_time = max(max_completion_time, completion_time)\n    \n    return max_completion_time\n```",
