      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef stringIndices(wordsContainer, wordsQuery):\n    # Create a list of (reversed_string, original_index, length) for all words in wordsContainer\n    # We reverse the strings to use prefix matching instead of suffix matching\n    container_reversed = [(word[::-1], i, len(word)) for i, word in enumerate(wordsContainer)]\n    \n    # Sort by reversed string to enable efficient prefix matching\n    container_reversed.sort()\n    \n    result = []\n    \n    for query in wordsQuery:\n        # Reverse the query string for prefix matching\n        reversed_query = query[::-1]\n        max_common_length = 0\n        best_index = 0\n        best_length = float('inf')\n        \n        # Check each word in container for common prefix (which is common suffix in original strings)\n        for rev_word, orig_idx, word_len in container_reversed:\n            # Find common prefix length\n            common_len = 0\n            min_len = min(len(reversed_query), len(rev_word))\n            for j in range(min_len):\n                if reversed_query[j] == rev_word[j]:\n                    common_len += 1\n                else:\n                    break\n            \n            # Update best match if this is better\n            if common_len > max_common_length:\n                max_common_length = common_len\n                best_index = orig_idx\n                best_length = word_len\n            elif common_len == max_common_length:\n                # If same common length, prefer shorter word\n                if word_len < best_length:\n                    best_index = orig_idx\n                    best_length = word_len\n                # If same length, prefer earlier occurrence (lower index)\n                elif word_len == best_length and orig_idx < best_index:\n                    best_index = orig_idx\n        \n        result.append(best_index)\n    \n    return result\n```",
