      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\n# Increase recursion depth just in case\nsys.setrecursionlimit(2000)\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from stdin efficiently\n    # sys.stdin.read().split() handles all whitespace (newlines, spaces) automatically\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    \n    if not input_data:\n        return\n\n    iterator = iter(input_data)\n    \n    try:\n        n_str = next(iterator)\n        N = int(n_str)\n        T_prime = next(iterator)\n    except StopIteration:\n        return\n\n    results = []\n    len_T = len(T_prime)\n    \n    # Iterate through each candidate string S_i\n    # Enumerate is range(1, N + 1) because output requires 1-based indices\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        try:\n            S = next(iterator)\n        except StopIteration:\n            break\n            \n        len_S = len(S)\n        is_valid = False\n        \n        # Case 1: S_i and T' have the same length\n        # Possible operations: T' equals T, or T' is obtained by changing one character in T.\n        if len_S == len_T:\n            if S == T_prime:\n                is_valid = True\n            else:\n                # Check if Hamming distance is exactly 1 (Change operation)\n                diff_count = 0\n                for s_char, t_char in zip(S, T_prime):\n                    if s_char != t_char:\n                        diff_count += 1\n                        if diff_count > 1:\n                            break\n                    # continue loop to find all differences\n                \n                if diff_count == 1:\n                    is_valid = True\n        \n        # Case 2: S_i is shorter than T' by 1 (Insertion operation)\n        # T' is obtained by inserting one character into T. \n        # Since we assume T = S_i, T' is S_i with one insertion.\n        elif len_S == len_T - 1:\n            m = None\n            # Find first mismatch\n            for k, (s_char, t_char) in enumerate(zip(S, T_prime)):\n                if s_char != t_char:\n                    m = k\n                    break\n            \n            if m is None:\n                # No mismatch found. S matches prefix of T'.\n                # Since len_T = len_S + 1, the extra char in T' is at the end.\n                is_valid = True\n            else:\n                # Mismatch at m. The char at T'[m] is the inserted character.\n                # We must verify that the rest of S matches the rest of T' (after insertion)\n                # i.e., T'[m+1:] == S[m:]\n                if S[m:] == T_prime[m+1:]:\n                    is_valid = True\n                    \n        # Case 3: S_i is longer than T' by 1 (Deletion operation)\n        # T' is obtained by deleting one character from T.\n        # Since we assume T = S_i, T' is S_i with one deletion.\n        elif len_S == len_T + 1:\n            m = None\n            # Find first mismatch\n            for k, (s_char, t_char) in enumerate(zip(S, T_prime)):\n                if s_char != t_char:\n                    m = k\n                    break\n            \n            if m is None:\n                # No mismatch found. S matches T' prefix + 1 extra char at end.\n                is_valid = True\n            else:\n                # Mismatch at m. The char at S[m] is the deleted character.\n                # We must verify that the rest of S (after deletion) matches T'.\n                # i.e., S[m+1:] == T'[m:]\n                if S[m+1:] == T_prime[m:]:\n                    is_valid = True\n        \n        if is_valid:\n            results.append(i)\n            \n    K = len(results)\n    print(K)\n    if K > 0:\n        print(*(results))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    solve()\n```",
