      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    # Parse first line\n    H = int(data[0])\n    W = int(data[1])\n    N = int(data[2])\n    \n    # Read holed squares\n    holed = set()\n    index = 3\n    for _ in range(N):\n        a = int(data[index])\n        b = int(data[index + 1])\n        holed.add((a, b))\n        index += 2\n    \n    count = 0\n    \n    # For each possible top-left corner\n    for i in range(1, H + 1):\n        for j in range(1, W + 1):\n            # Check all possible sizes n starting from 1\n            max_n = min(H - i + 1, W - j + 1)\n            for n in range(1, max_n + 1):\n                # Check if the n×n square from (i,j) has any holed squares\n                is_holeless = True\n                for k in range(n):\n                    for l in range(n):\n                        if (i + k, j + l) in holed:\n                            is_holeless = False\n                            break\n                    if not is_holeless:\n                        break\n                \n                if is_holeless:\n                    count += 1\n                else:\n                    # If an n×n square has a hole, then any larger square starting at (i,j) will also have a hole\n                    break\n    \n    print(count)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
