    "global index": "LiveCodeBench_494",
    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nYou are given a string s, which is known to be a concatenation of anagrams of some string t.\nReturn the minimum possible length of the string t.\nAn anagram is formed by rearranging the letters of a string. For example, \"aab\", \"aba\", and, \"baa\" are anagrams of \"aab\".\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: s = \"abba\"\nOutput: 2\nExplanation:\nOne possible string t could be \"ba\".\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: s = \"cdef\"\nOutput: 4\nExplanation:\nOne possible string t could be \"cdef\", notice that t can be equal to s.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= s.length <= 10^5\ns consist only of lowercase English letters.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the minimum possible length of string t such that s is a concatenation of anagrams of t.\n\nKey insights:\n1. If s is made of k anagrams of t, then len(s) = k * len(t)\n2. So len(t) must be a divisor of len(s)\n3. For each possible length L (that divides len(s)), I need to check if s can be split into segments of length L where all segments are anagrams of each other\n4. I want the minimum possible L\n\nTo check if a length L works:\n- Divide s into segments of length L\n- All segments must have the same character frequency (i.e., they're anagrams)\n- Count character frequency of first segment, then verify all other segments have the same frequency\n\n```python\ndef solve(s):\n    n = len(s)\n    \n    # Try all possible lengths that divide n\n    for length in range(1, n + 1):\n        if n % length == 0:\n            k = n // length  # number of segments\n            \n            # Get frequency of first segment\n            first_freq = [0] * 26\n            for i in range(length):\n                first_freq[ord(s[i]) - ord('a')] += 1\n            \n            # Check if all other segments have the same frequency\n            valid = True\n            for seg in range(1, k):\n                seg_freq = [0] * 26\n                start = seg * length\n                for i in range(start, start + length):\n                    seg_freq[ord(s[i]) - ord('a')] += 1\n                \n                if seg_freq != first_freq:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            \n            if valid:\n                return length\n    \n    return n  # fallback (should never reach here)\n```",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
