      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef solve():\n    n = int(input())\n    points = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        x, y = map(int, input().split())\n        points.append((x, y))\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        max_distance = -1\n        farthest_id = n + 1  # Initialize with a value larger than any possible ID\n        \n        for j in range(n):\n            if i == j:\n                continue\n                \n            # Calculate Euclidean distance\n            distance = math.sqrt((points[i][0] - points[j][0])**2 + (points[i][1] - points[j][1])**2)\n            \n            # Update farthest point if this one is farther, or has smaller ID with same distance\n            if distance > max_distance or (distance == max_distance and j + 1 < farthest_id):\n                max_distance = distance\n                farthest_id = j + 1  # +1 because IDs are 1-indexed\n        \n        print(farthest_id)\n\nsolve()\n```",
