\nLet \\( G(x,y) = 2 \\cdot F(x,y) = x y + (x \\% 2) \\cdot (y \\% 2) \\).\n\nThen:\n\\[\n\\text{answer} = G(C,D) - G(A,D) - G(C,B) + G(A,B)\n\\]\nwhere \\( G(x,y) = x y + (x \\% 2) \\cdot (y \\% 2) \\).\n\n---\n\n### 8. Implementation\n\nWe implement \\( G(x,y) \\) using modulo 2, but careful with negative numbers:  \nIn Python, `x % 2` is 0 or 1 for non-negative, but for negative odd, it’s 1? Wait, -3 % 2 = 1 in Python. So it’s fine: (x % 2) is 1 if x odd, 0 if x even, for any integer.\n\nSo formula works for negatives too.\n\n---\n\nHere’s the Python implementation:\n\n```python\ndef G(x, y):\n    return x * y + (x % 2) * (y % 2)\n\ndef main():\n    A, B, C, D = map(int, input().split())\n    ans = G(C, D) - G(A, D) - G(C, B) + G(A, B)\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
