\nSo total characters = 2 * (2*min(x,y) + (1 if x != y else 0)) + 2*z = 4*min(x,y) + 2*(1 if x != y else 0) + 2*z\n\nBut let me check:\n- ex1: 4*min(2,5) + 2*1 + 2*1 = 8 + 2 + 2 = 12 ✓\n- ex2: 4*min(3,2) + 2*1 + 2*2 = 8 + 2 + 4 = 14 ✓\n\nPerfect! So the formula is 2*z + 4*min(x,y) + 2*(x != y)\n\nBut wait, let me verify the reasoning: \n- I can use 2*min(x,y) \"AA\" and \"BB\" strings in alternating pairs (4*min(x,y) chars)\n- If x != y, I can use one additional string (the excess one) (2 more chars)  \n- I can use all z \"AB\" strings (2*z chars)\n\nYes, that makes sense.\n\n```python\ndef solution(x, y, z):\n    return 2 * z + 4 * min(x, y) + 2 * (1 if x != y else 0)\n```",
