      "generated_answer": "We can treat this as a shortest-path problem between the start, goal, and candies, but we need to maximize candies collected within a move limit.  \n\nSince there are at most 18 candies, we can:  \n\n1. Find all important points: start, goal, candies.  \n2. Compute shortest distances between all pairs of important points using BFS.  \n3. Use dynamic programming over subsets of candies to find the best route that starts at `S`, ends at `G`, and has total moves ≤ `T`.  \n\nHere’s the implementation:  \n\n```python\nfrom sys import stdin\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef main():\n    H, W, T = map(int, stdin.readline().split())\n    grid = [stdin.readline().strip() for _ in range(H)]\n\n    # Locate start, goal, and candies\n    start = goal = None\n    candies = []\n    pos_to_id = {}\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == 'S':\n                start = (i, j)\n            elif grid[i][j] == 'G':\n                goal = (i, j)\n            elif grid[i][j] == 'o':\n                candies.append((i, j))\n\n    # Assign IDs: 0 = start, then candies, then goal\n    points = [start] + candies + [goal]\n    n = len(points)\n    candy_count = len(candies)\n\n    for idx, pt in enumerate(points):\n        pos_to_id[pt] = idx\n\n    # BFS from each important point to compute pairwise distances\n    INF = 10 ** 9\n    dist_matrix = [[INF] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Directions\n    dirs = [(1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1)]\n\n    for idx, (sy, sx) in enumerate(points):\n        dq = deque()\n        dist = [[-1] * W for _ in range(H)]\n        dist[sy][sx] = 0\n        dq.append((sy, sx))\n        while dq:\n            y, x = dq.popleft()\n            for dy, dx in dirs:\n                ny, nx = y + dy, x + dx\n                if 0 <= ny < H and 0 <= nx < W and grid[ny][nx] != '#':\n                    if dist[ny][nx] == -1:\n                        dist[ny][nx] = dist[y][x] + 1\n                        dq.append((ny, nx))\n        # Fill dist_matrix[idx][other]\n        for j, (ty, tx) in enumerate(points):\n            d = dist[ty][tx]\n            if d == -1:\n                dist_matrix[idx][j] = INF\n            else:\n                dist_matrix[idx][j] = d\n\n    # If direct start to goal is impossible or too long, check later\n    if dist_matrix[0][n - 1] > T:\n        # Might still be possible via candies, but if unreachable, print -1\n        if dist_matrix[0][n - 1] == INF:\n            print(-1)\n            return\n\n    # DP[mask][last] = min moves to visit candy set 'mask' ending at 'last'\n    # last: 0..candy_count-1 (candy indices), start is separate\n    # We'll index candies as 1..candy_count in points list\n    # Actually: points[0]=start, points[1..candy_count]=candies, points[candy_count+1]=goal\n    # So candy indices in DP: 0..candy_count-1\n    # DP size: 2^candy_count * candy_count\n    if candy_count == 0:\n        # No candies, just check start->goal\n        if dist_matrix[0][1] <= T:\n            print(0)\n        else:\n            print(-1)\n        return\n\n    DP = [[INF] * candy_count for _ in range(1 << candy_count)]\n\n    # Start from S to each candy\n    for i in range(candy_count):\n        d = dist_matrix[0][i + 1]  # i+1 because points[0]=start, points[1..]=candies\n        if d < INF:\n            DP[1 << i][i] = d\n\n    # DP transition\n    for mask in range(1 << candy_count):\n        for last in range(candy_count):\n            if DP[mask][last] >= INF:\n                continue\n            # Try next candy\n            for nxt in range(candy_count):\n                if mask >> nxt & 1:\n                    continue\n                nd = DP[mask][last] + dist_matrix[last + 1][nxt + 1]\n                if nd < DP[mask | (1 << nxt)][nxt]:\n                    DP[mask | (1 << nxt)][nxt] = nd\n\n    ans = -1\n    # Check each subset of candies\n    for mask in range(1 << candy_count):\n        for last in range(candy_count):\n            if DP[mask][last] >= INF:\n                continue\n            # Go to goal\n            total_moves = DP[mask][last] + dist_matrix[last + 1][n - 1]\n            if total_moves <= T:\n                cnt = bin(mask).count(\"1\")\n                ans = max(ans, cnt)\n\n    # Also check direct start->goal without candies\n    if dist_matrix[0][n - 1] <= T:\n        ans = max(ans, 0)\n\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
