    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the length of the longest common prefix between any pair of integers where one comes from arr1 and the other from arr2.\n\nThe key insight is that I need to:\n1. For each number in arr1, generate all its prefixes\n2. For each number in arr2, generate all its prefixes\n3. Find the longest common prefix that appears in both sets\n\nI can do this efficiently by:\n- Converting each number to a string to work with its digits\n- Generating all prefixes for numbers in arr1 and storing them in a set\n- For each number in arr2, checking its prefixes against the set from arr1\n- Tracking the maximum length of any common prefix found\n\n```python\ndef longestCommonPrefix(arr1, arr2):\n    # Store all prefixes from arr1\n    prefixes1 = set()\n    \n    for num in arr1:\n        num_str = str(num)\n        # Generate all prefixes of the number\n        for i in range(1, len(num_str) + 1):\n            prefixes1.add(num_str[:i])\n    \n    max_length = 0\n    \n    # Check all prefixes from arr2 against prefixes from arr1\n    for num in arr2:\n        num_str = str(num)\n        # Check each prefix of the current number\n        for i in range(1, len(num_str) + 1):\n            prefix = num_str[:i]\n            if prefix in prefixes1:\n                max_length = max(max_length, len(prefix))\n    \n    return max_length\n```",
