      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef semiOrderedPermutation(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    # Find positions of 1 and n\n    pos_1 = nums.index(1)\n    pos_n = nums.index(n)\n    \n    # Calculate minimum operations\n    # Operations needed to move 1 to first position: pos_1\n    # Operations needed to move n to last position: (n - 1 - pos_n)\n    operations = pos_1 + (n - 1 - pos_n)\n    \n    # If 1 is after n in the original array, we save one operation\n    # because when we move 1 forward past n, it effectively helps move n backward\n    if pos_1 > pos_n:\n        operations -= 1\n        \n    return operations\n```",
