      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    T = input().strip()\n    N = int(input().strip())\n    \n    bags = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        line = input().split()\n        A_i = int(line[0])\n        strings = line[1:A_i+1]\n        bags.append(strings)\n    \n    # dp[i] = minimum cost to make prefix T[:i] (i characters)\n    n = len(T)\n    INF = float('inf')\n    dp = [INF] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0  # Empty string costs 0\n    \n    # Process each bag in order\n    for bag_strings in bags:\n        # Create a new dp array for the state after processing this bag\n        new_dp = dp[:]\n        \n        # For each possible current position in T\n        for i in range(n + 1):\n            if dp[i] == INF:\n                continue\n                \n            # Try each string in the current bag\n            for s in bag_strings:\n                # Check if we can append s to T[:i] to get a prefix of T\n                if i + len(s) <= n and T[i:i+len(s)] == s:\n                    new_dp[i + len(s)] = min(new_dp[i + len(s)], dp[i] + 1)\n        \n        dp = new_dp\n    \n    print(dp[n] if dp[n] != INF else -1)\n\nsolve()\n```",
