    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Looking at the problem, we need to compute the sum of distances weighted by given coefficients \\( C_i \\) for each vertex, and then find the minimum among all vertices.\n\nWe have a tree with \\( N \\) vertices, and for each vertex \\( x \\) we want:\n\n\\[\nf(x) = \\sum_{i=1}^{N} C_i \\cdot d(x, i)\n\\]\n\nwhere \\( d(x, i) \\) is the number of edges between vertices \\( x \\) and \\( i \\).\n\nWe want \\(\\min_{1 \\leq v \\leq N} f(v)\\).\n\n---\n\n## Approach\n\nThis is similar to computing **weighted distance sums** on a tree.  \nIf we think of \\( C_i \\) as weights at each vertex, \\( f(x) \\) is the total weighted distance from \\( x \\) to all vertices.\n\nWe can compute \\( f(x) \\) for all vertices efficiently using **tree DP and rerooting**.\n\nLet’s define:\n\n- Let \\( dp[v] \\) be the sum of weighted distances from vertex \\( v \\) to all vertices in its subtree when rooted at \\( v \\) during DFS.\n- Let \\( sum[v] \\) be the sum of weights \\( C_i \\) in the subtree of \\( v \\) (for the same rooting).\n\nThen, we can compute \\( f(1) \\) easily with DFS from a chosen root (say vertex 1).  \nAfter that, we can propagate the values to children using rerooting formulas.\n\n---\n\n### Rerooting formula\n\nIf we know \\( f(u) \\) for a vertex \\( u \\) (parent), and want \\( f(v) \\) for child \\( v \\) of \\( u \\):\n\nWe have:\n\\[\nf(v) = f(u) - sum[v] \\cdot 1 + (total\\_sum - sum[v]) \\cdot 1\n\\]\nWait — let’s derive carefully.\n\nWhen moving root from \\( u \\) to \\( v \\):\n\n- For nodes in subtree of \\( v \\), their distance to new root \\( v \\) is decreased by 1 compared to distance to \\( u \\).\n- For nodes outside subtree of \\( v \\) (including \\( u \\) and others), their distance to new root \\( v \\) is increased by 1 compared to distance to \\( u \\).\n\nSo:\n\\[\nf(v) = f(u) - \\text{(sum of weights in subtree of \\( v \\)} + \\text{(sum of weights outside subtree of \\( v \\)}\n\\]\n\nLet \\( subtree\\_sum[v] \\) be total \\( C \\) in subtree of \\( v \\) when rooted at \\( u \\) (parent).  \nLet \\( total\\_sum = \\sum_{i=1}^N C_i \\).\n\nThen:\n\\[\nf(v) = f(u) - subtree\\_sum[v] + (total\\_sum - subtree\\_sum[v])\n\\]\n\\[\nf(v) = f(u) + total\\_sum - 2 \\cdot subtree\\_sum[v]\n\\]\n\nYes, that’s correct.\n\n---\n\n### Algorithm steps:\n\n1. Pick root = 1.\n2. First DFS: compute:\n   - \\( subtree\\_sum[v] \\) = sum of \\( C \\) in subtree.\n   - \\( dp[v] \\) = sum of weighted distances from \\( v \\) to all vertices in its subtree.\n     Actually, we can compute \\( f(1) \\) directly:\n     \\( f(1) = \\sum_{i} C_i \\cdot \\text{distance}(1, i) \\) by DFS from root 1.\n     But for rerooting, we need \\( subtree\\_sum \\) anyway.\n\n3. Compute \\( f(1) \\) with DFS:  \n   Let \\( dist[v] \\) = distance from root to \\( v \\), then \\( f(1) = \\sum_v C_v \\cdot dist[v] \\).\n\n4. Second DFS (rerooting):  \n   Using formula \\( f(v) = f(u) + total\\_sum - 2 \\cdot subtree\\_sum[v] \\) when moving from parent \\( u \\) to child \\( v \\).\n\n5. Track the minimum \\( f(v) \\) over all vertices.\n\n---\n\n### Implementation details:\n\n- We need adjacency list for tree.\n- We avoid recursion depth issues by using iterative DFS or sys.setrecursionlimit for \\( N \\) up to \\( 10^5 \\).\n\n---\n\nHere’s the implementation:\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\nsys.setrecursionlimit(300000)\n\ndef solve():\n    input = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    N = int(input[0])\n    edges = []\n    idx = 1\n    for _ in range(N - 1):\n        a = int(input[idx])\n        b = int(input[idx + 1])\n        idx += 2\n        edges.append((a - 1, b - 1))\n    C = list(map(int, input[idx:idx + N]))\n    idx += N\n\n    # Build adjacency list\n    adj = [[] for _ in range(N)]\n    for a, b in edges:\n        adj[a].append(b)\n        adj[b].append(a)\n\n    total_sum = sum(C)\n\n    # First DFS to compute subtree_sum and f_root\n    subtree_sum = [0] * N\n    parent = [-1] * N\n    order = []\n    stack = [(0, -1, 0)]  # (node, parent, dist)\n    dist_from_root = [0] * N\n    while stack:\n        u, p, d = stack.pop()\n        parent[u] = p\n        dist_from_root[u] = d\n        order.append(u)\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if v != p:\n                stack.append((v, u, d + 1))\n\n    # Compute subtree_sum in reverse order\n    for u in reversed(order):\n        subtree_sum[u] = C[u]\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if v != parent[u]:\n                subtree_sum[u] += subtree_sum[v]\n\n    # Compute f(1)\n    f_root = 0\n    for u in range(N):\n        f_root += C[u] * dist_from_root[u]\n\n    f = [0] * N\n    f[0] = f_root\n\n    # Rerooting DFS\n    stack = [(0, -1)]\n    while stack:\n        u, p = stack.pop()\n        for v in adj[u]:\n            if v != p:\n                f[v] = f[u] + total_sum - 2 * subtree_sum[v]\n                stack.append((v, u))\n\n    # Find minimum\n    ans = min(f)\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
