    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countCompleteSubstrings(word, k):\n    def count_substrings(s, k):\n        n = len(s)\n        if n < k:\n            return 0\n        \n        result = 0\n        \n        # Iterate over possible substring lengths: k, 2k, 3k, ..., 26k (at most 26 unique chars)\n        for num_chars in range(1, 27):\n            length = num_chars * k\n            if length > n:\n                break\n                \n            # Use sliding window of size 'length'\n            char_count = {}\n            \n            # Initialize first window\n            for i in range(length):\n                char_count[s[i]] = char_count.get(s[i], 0) + 1\n            \n            # Check if current window is valid\n            if is_valid_substring(char_count, k):\n                result += 1\n            \n            # Slide the window\n            for i in range(length, n):\n                # Add new character\n                char_count[s[i]] = char_count.get(s[i], 0) + 1\n                # Remove old character\n                char_count[s[i - length]] -= 1\n                if char_count[s[i - length]] == 0:\n                    del char_count[s[i - length]]\n                \n                # Check if current window is valid\n                if is_valid_substring(char_count, k):\n                    result += 1\n        \n        return result\n    \n    def is_valid_substring(char_count, k):\n        # Check if each character appears exactly k times\n        for count in char_count.values():\n            if count != k:\n                return False\n        return True\n    \n    def is_adjacent_valid(s):\n        # Check if difference between adjacent characters is at most 2\n        for i in range(len(s) - 1):\n            if abs(ord(s[i]) - ord(s[i + 1])) > 2:\n                return False\n        return True\n    \n    result = 0\n    n = len(word)\n    \n    # Split the string at positions where adjacent characters differ by more than 2\n    start = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if abs(ord(word[i]) - ord(word[i-1])) > 2:\n            # Process the segment from start to i\n            segment = word[start:i]\n            result += count_substrings(segment, k)\n            start = i\n    \n    # Process the last segment\n    segment = word[start:]\n    result += count_substrings(segment, k)\n    \n    return result\n```",
