      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef shortestBeautifulSubstring(s, k):\n    n = len(s)\n    min_length = float('inf')\n    candidates = []\n    \n    # Find all beautiful substrings and track the minimum length\n    for i in range(n):\n        ones_count = 0\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            if s[j] == '1':\n                ones_count += 1\n            \n            # If we have exactly k ones, we found a beautiful substring\n            if ones_count == k:\n                length = j - i + 1\n                if length < min_length:\n                    min_length = length\n                    candidates = [s[i:j+1]]\n                elif length == min_length:\n                    candidates.append(s[i:j+1])\n                break\n    \n    # If no beautiful substring found\n    if min_length == float('inf'):\n        return \"\"\n    \n    # Return lexicographically smallest substring\n    return min(candidates)\n```",
