    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minSizeSubarray(nums, target):\n    n = len(nums)\n    total_sum = sum(nums)\n    \n    # If target is greater than total_sum, we can use complete cycles of nums\n    min_length = 0\n    if target > total_sum:\n        cycles = target // total_sum\n        min_length += cycles * n\n        target %= total_sum\n    \n    # If target becomes 0 after removing complete cycles\n    if target == 0:\n        return min_length\n    \n    # Now we need to find a subarray in the circular array with sum = target\n    # We can use sliding window on nums appended to itself (at most 2 copies needed)\n    double_nums = nums + nums\n    left = 0\n    current_sum = 0\n    min_window = float('inf')\n    \n    for right in range(len(double_nums)):\n        current_sum += double_nums[right]\n        \n        while current_sum > target and left <= right:\n            current_sum -= double_nums[left]\n            left += 1\n            \n        if current_sum == target:\n            min_window = min(min_window, right - left + 1)\n    \n    return min_length + min_window if min_window != float('inf') else -1\n```",
