    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\n# Increase recursion depth just in case, though iterative solution is used\nsys.setrecursionlimit(2000)\n\ndef main():\n    # Read all input from standard input efficiently\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    \n    if not input_data:\n        return\n\n    iterator = iter(input_data)\n    try:\n        # Read N and Q\n        N = int(next(iterator))\n        Q = int(next(iterator))\n\n        # Initialize boxes. We use a list of sets to store the colors in each box.\n        # Indices are 1 to N. boxes[i] is the set of colors in box i.\n        # Python sets handle distinct values automatically.\n        boxes = [set() for _ in range(N + 1)]\n\n        # Read initial colors for each box\n        for i in range(1, N + 1):\n            c_val = int(next(iterator))\n            boxes[i].add(c_val)\n\n        output = []\n        \n        # Process queries\n        for _ in range(Q):\n            a = int(next(iterator))\n            b = int(next(iterator))\n\n            # Get references to the sets in boxes a and b\n            set_a = boxes[a]\n            set_b = boxes[b]\n\n            # We want to move balls from a to b.\n            # This is equivalent to merging the set of colors of a into b.\n            # To ensure efficiency (small-to-large merging), we merge the smaller set into the larger set.\n            \n            if len(set_a) <= len(set_b):\n                # Case 1: set_a is smaller or equal.\n                # We update set_b with elements of set_a.\n                # This takes time proportional to len(set_a).\n                set_b.update(set_a)\n                # Box a is now empty.\n                boxes[a] = set()\n                # Box b now holds the union.\n                output.append(str(len(set_b)))\n                \n            else:\n                # Case 2: set_a is larger.\n                # We update set_a with elements of set_b.\n                # This takes time proportional to len(set_b).\n                set_a.update(set_b)\n                # Box b must now hold the union (which is in set_a).\n                # So we assign set_a to boxes[b].\n                boxes[b] = set_a\n                # Box a becomes empty.\n                boxes[a] = set()\n                # Box b now points to the updated set_a.\n                output.append(str(len(set_a)))\n\n        # Print all outputs\n        sys.stdout.write('\\n'.join(output) + '\\n')\n\n    except StopIteration:\n        pass\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```",
