      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve(nums, freq):\n    \"\"\"\n    Track the frequency of IDs in a collection that changes over time.\n    \n    Args:\n        nums: List of integers representing IDs\n        freq: List of integers representing frequency changes\n    \n    Returns:\n        List of integers where each element represents the count of the most \n        frequent ID after each step\n    \"\"\"\n    # Dictionary to store current frequency count of each ID\n    count = {}\n    # Result array to store maximum frequency after each step\n    ans = []\n    \n    for i in range(len(nums)):\n        # Get current ID and its frequency change\n        id_val = nums[i]\n        change = freq[i]\n        \n        # Update the count for the current ID\n        if id_val not in count:\n            count[id_val] = 0\n        count[id_val] += change\n        \n        # Find the maximum frequency in the current collection\n        if count:\n            max_freq = max(count.values())\n            # Only add if max_freq > 0, otherwise collection is empty\n            ans.append(max_freq if max_freq > 0 else 0)\n        else:\n            ans.append(0)\n    \n    return ans\n```",
