      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef beautifulIndices(s: str, a: str, b: str, k: int) -> list:\n    # Find all indices where string 'a' appears in 's'\n    a_indices = []\n    for i in range(len(s) - len(a) + 1):\n        if s[i:i + len(a)] == a:\n            a_indices.append(i)\n    \n    # Find all indices where string 'b' appears in 's'\n    b_indices = []\n    for i in range(len(s) - len(b) + 1):\n        if s[i:i + len(b)] == b:\n            b_indices.append(i)\n    \n    # Check for beautiful indices\n    beautiful = []\n    for i in a_indices:\n        # For each occurrence of 'a', check if there's a 'b' occurrence within distance k\n        for j in b_indices:\n            if abs(j - i) <= k:\n                beautiful.append(i)\n                break  # Once we find one valid j for this i, we can stop\n    \n    return beautiful\n```",
