      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef getLastVisitedIntegers(words: List[str]) -> List[int]:\n    seen_integers = []\n    result = []\n    consecutive_prev_count = 0\n\n    for word in words:\n        if word == \"prev\":\n            consecutive_prev_count += 1\n            if consecutive_prev_count > len(seen_integers):\n                result.append(-1)\n            else:\n                # nums_reverse is reversed(seen_integers)\n                # We need the element at index (consecutive_prev_count - 1)\n                # In terms of forward indexing of seen_integers, this is:\n                # len(seen_integers) - consecutive_prev_count\n                idx = len(seen_integers) - consecutive_prev_count\n                result.append(seen_integers[idx])\n        else:\n            seen_integers.append(int(word))\n            consecutive_prev_count = 0\n            \n    return result\n```",
