      "generated_answer": "Looking at this problem, I need to find the minimum number of coins to add so that all integers from 1 to target are obtainable.\n\nThe key insight is to use a greedy approach. I'll maintain the range of obtainable values [1, max_obtainable] and extend it step by step.\n\nThe strategy:\n1. Sort the coins\n2. Keep track of the maximum obtainable value so far\n3. For each position, if there's a gap between current max_obtainable and the next coin, add a coin of value (max_obtainable + 1) to fill the gap\n4. When we add a coin of value v, the new max obtainable becomes max_obtainable + v\n5. Continue until max_obtainable >= target\n\nHere's the solution:\n\n```python\ndef minimumAddedCoins(coins, target):\n    coins.sort()\n    max_obtainable = 0\n    added_coins = 0\n    i = 0\n    \n    while max_obtainable < target:\n        # If there's a coin that can extend our range, use it\n        if i < len(coins) and coins[i] <= max_obtainable + 1:\n            max_obtainable += coins[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            # Need to add a new coin of value max_obtainable + 1\n            new_coin = max_obtainable + 1\n            max_obtainable += new_coin\n            added_coins += 1\n    \n    return added_coins\n```",
