      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    # Read input\n    N = int(data[0])\n    K = int(data[1])\n    P = list(map(int, data[2:2+N]))\n    \n    # For K = 1, the answer is always 0\n    if K == 1:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    # Create position array: pos[i] = index (1-indexed) where value i appears in P\n    pos = [0] * (N + 1)\n    for i in range(N):\n        pos[P[i]] = i + 1  # 1-indexed position\n    \n    min_diff = float('inf')\n    \n    # Check all possible consecutive sequences of K integers\n    # i.e., {a, a+1, ..., a+K-1} for a from 1 to N-K+1\n    for a in range(1, N - K + 2):\n        # Get positions of all values in the consecutive sequence\n        positions = []\n        for j in range(a, a + K):\n            positions.append(pos[j])\n        \n        # Sort positions to find the minimum and maximum index\n        positions.sort()\n        # The difference is last index - first index (i_K - i_1)\n        diff = positions[-1] - positions[0]\n        min_diff = min(min_diff, diff)\n    \n    print(min_diff)\n\nsolve()\n```",
