    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read all input from stdin\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    \n    # Parse N, M\n    N = int(input_data[0])\n    M = int(input_data[1])\n    \n    # Parse string S\n    S = list(input_data[2])\n    \n    # Parse colors C\n    C = [int(input_data[3 + i]) - 1 for i in range(N)]  # Convert to 0-indexed\n    \n    # Track positions for each color (0-indexed color)\n    color_positions = [[] for _ in range(M)]\n    for i, color in enumerate(C):\n        color_positions[color].append(i)\n    \n    # For each color in order, perform right circular shift\n    for color in range(M):\n        positions = color_positions[color]\n        if len(positions) <= 1:\n            continue\n        \n        # Get characters at these positions\n        chars = [S[pos] for pos in positions]\n        \n        # Right circular shift: last character moves to front\n        # For characters [0, 1, 2, ..., k-1], after right shift: [k-1, 0, 1, ..., k-2]\n        # Update string S at those positions\n        S[positions[-1]] = chars[0]  # Last original position gets first char\n        for i in range(len(positions) - 1):\n            S[positions[i]] = chars[i + 1]  # Each position gets next char\n    \n    # Print the result\n    print(''.join(S))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```",
