      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef getSmallestString(s, k):\n    if k == 0:\n        return s\n    \n    result = []\n    remaining_k = k\n    \n    for char in s:\n        current_ord = ord(char) - ord('a')\n        \n        # Calculate minimum distance from 'a'\n        dist_to_a = min(current_ord, 26 - current_ord)\n        \n        if dist_to_a <= remaining_k:\n            # We can change this character to 'a'\n            result.append('a')\n            remaining_k -= dist_to_a\n        else:\n            # We can't reach 'a', so move as close as possible\n            # towards 'a' in lexicographical order\n            if current_ord <= 13:  # closer to 'a' going backward\n                new_char_ord = current_ord - remaining_k\n                result.append(chr(new_char_ord + ord('a')))\n                remaining_k = 0\n            else:  # closer to 'a' going forward through cycle\n                # In this case, going forward would take us away from lexicographically smallest\n                # So we go backward\n                new_char_ord = current_ord - remaining_k\n                result.append(chr(new_char_ord + ord('a')))\n                remaining_k = 0\n    \n    return ''.join(result)\n```",
