      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef lexicographically_smallest_array(nums, limit):\n    n = len(nums)\n    sorted_nums = sorted(nums)\n\n    # Build connected components of values\n    # A component is a maximal set of values where each adjacent value in sorted order\n    # differs from its predecessor by at most `limit`.\n    groups = []\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    group_start = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if sorted_nums[i] - sorted_nums[i - 1] > limit:\n            groups.append(tuple(sorted_nums[group_start:i]))\n            group_start = i\n    groups.append(tuple(sorted_nums[group_start:]))\n\n    # Group indices in the original array by which component each value belongs\n    # Map: value -> component index\n    value_to_component = {}\n    for comp_idx, group in enumerate(groups):\n        for val in group:\n            value_to_component[val] = comp_idx\n\n    # For each position in original array, find the component and collect elements\n    components_to_positions = [[] for _ in groups]\n    original_pos = []  # to map sorted value to original position\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        comp_idx = value_to_component[nums[i]]\n        group_values = groups[comp_idx]\n        # Keep track of which sorted value occupies which component position\n        original_index_map = {val: i for i, val in enumerate(group_values)}\n\n    result = list(nums)\n\n    # For each component, collect all values at original positions and sort them\n    # to get lexicographically smallest arrangement for that group\n    for comp_idx in range(len(groups)):\n        group = list(groups[comp_idx])\n        # Find positions where this component's values are currently located\n        positions = []\n        for i in range(n):\n            comp = value_to_component[result[i]]  # re-check with current array\n            if comp == comp_idx:\n                positions.append(i)\n\n        # Sort group elements to get new values for these positions\n        sorted_values = sorted(group)\n\n        # Place sorted values back to positions (in original index order)\n        for idx, new_val in zip(positions, sorted_values):\n            result[idx] = new_val\n\n    return result\n```",
