ked[index] = True\n        \n        # Mark k smallest unmarked elements\n        _count, _k = 0, k\n        while _count < _k and heap:\n            val, idx = heapq.heappop(heap)\n            if marked[idx]:\n                continue\n            total_sum -= val\n            marked[idx] = True\n            _count += 1\n        \n        answer.append(total_sum)\n    \n    return answer\n```\n\n### Key Features:\n- Tracks marked elements via a boolean array\n- Uses min-heap to always find the smallest unmarked element by value and index\n- Updates the current sum of unmarked elements as each operation removes marked elements from it\n- Lazy removal from the heap ensures that elements marked explicitly in a query are not processed again\n\nThis implementation satisfies the constraints efficiently in O(mn log n) worst-case time, which fits within the problem's bounds for n up to 10^5.",
