    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    M = int(input().strip())\n    S1 = input().strip()\n    S2 = input().strip()\n    S3 = input().strip()\n    \n    reels = [S1, S2, S3]\n    \n    min_time = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try each digit from 0 to 9\n    for digit in '0123456789':\n        times = []  # For each reel, find the earliest time that shows this digit\n        \n        for reel in reels:\n            reel_times = []\n            # Find all positions in the reel where this digit appears\n            for pos in range(M):\n                if reel[pos] == digit:\n                    reel_times.append(pos)\n            \n            # If digit doesn't appear in this reel, it's impossible\n            if not reel_times:\n                times = None\n                break\n                \n            times.append(reel_times)\n        \n        if times is None:  # This digit doesn't appear in all reels\n            continue\n            \n        # Try all combinations of times to stop each reel\n        # We need to assign a distinct time (or same time if possible) to each reel\n        # such that we minimize the maximum time\n        for t1 in times[0]:\n            for t2 in times[1]:\n                for t3 in times[2]:\n                    # We can press buttons at different times t1, t2, t3\n                    # But we need to make sure we can press them in some order\n                    # The total time is the maximum time we press any button\n                    # Since we can press at most one button per second,\n                    # we need to make sure we don't press two buttons at the same time\n                    # except that we can press only one button per second\n                    # So the time when we finish is max(t1, t2, t3)\n                    \n                    # However, we need to make sure we don't press two buttons at the same time\n                    # So if any two times are the same, we need to reschedule\n                    times_list = sorted([t1, t2, t3])\n                    actual_times = [0, 0, 0]\n                    \n                    # Assign actual times ensuring no two buttons are pressed at the same second\n                    actual_times[0] = times_list[0]  # Earliest time can be at its scheduled time\n                    actual_times[1] = max(times_list[1], actual_times[0] + 1)  # Next button at least 1 second later\n                    actual_times[2] = max(times_list[2], actual_times[1] + 1)  # Last button at least 1 second after the second\n                    \n                    # Map back to original order\n                    final_times = [0, 0, 0]\n                    sorted_indices = sorted(range(3), key=lambda i: [t1, t2, t3][i])\n                    \n                    for i, idx in enumerate(sorted_indices):\n                        final_times[idx] = actual_times[i]\n                    \n                    # The total time is the maximum of the actual pressing times\n                    total_time = max(final_times)\n                    min_time = min(min_time, total_time)\n    \n    if min_time == float('inf'):\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        print(min_time)\n\nsolve()\n```",
