      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef maximumJumps(nums, target):\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    # dp[i] represents the maximum number of jumps to reach index i\n    # Initialize with -1 (unreachable)\n    dp = [-1] * n\n    \n    # Base case: we start at index 0, so 0 jumps needed to reach index 0\n    dp[0] = 0\n    \n    # Fill the dp array\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        for i in range(j):\n            # Check if we can jump from i to j\n            if dp[i] != -1 and -target <= nums[j] - nums[i] <= target:\n                # If we can reach i, and the jump condition is satisfied\n                # Update dp[j] with maximum jumps\n                if dp[j] == -1:\n                    dp[j] = dp[i] + 1\n                else:\n                    dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[i] + 1)\n    \n    return dp[n-1]\n```",
