      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve(s1: str, s2: str, s3: str) -> int:\n    # If the first characters don't match, they can never be made equal\n    if s1[0] != s2[0] or s2[0] != s3[0]:\n        return -1\n    \n    # Find the longest common prefix among the three strings\n    min_len = min(len(s1), len(s2), len(s3))\n    common_prefix_len = 0\n    \n    for i in range(min_len):\n        if s1[i] == s2[i] == s3[i]:\n            common_prefix_len += 1\n        else:\n            break\n    \n    # Calculate the number of operations needed\n    # Operations = total length - (common prefix length * 3)\n    operations = (len(s1) - common_prefix_len) + (len(s2) - common_prefix_len) + (len(s3) - common_prefix_len)\n    \n    return operations\n```",
