    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A particular disk unit uses a bit string to record the occupancy or vacancy of its tracks, with O denoting vacant and 1 denoting occupied. A 32-bit segment of this string has the hexadecimal value D4FE2003. The percentage of occupied tracks for the corresponding part of the disk, to the nearest percent, is\n\nOptions: \nA. 69%\nB. 38%\nC. 12%\nD. 50%\nE. 25%\nF. 75%\nG. 44%\nH. 62%\nI. 56%\nJ. 81%\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, convert D4FE2003 from hex to binary:  \nD = 1101, 4 = 0100, F = 1111, E = 1110, 2 = 0010, 0 = 0000, 0 = 0000, 3 = 0011.  \nSo binary is 1101 0100 1111 1110 0010 0000 0000 0011.  \n\nCount the 1’s (occupied tracks): D4FE → 8+3+4+6=21 ones, 2003 → 1+2=3 ones, total = 24 ones.  \n\nTotal bits = 32, so percentage occupied = 24/32 = 75%.  \n\nThis matches option F.  \n\n\\boxed{F}",
