    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We have:  \n\\( P(A) = \\frac12 \\), \\( P(B) = \\frac13 \\), \\( P(\\neg B) = 1 - \\frac13 = \\frac23 \\), and \\( P(A | \\neg B) = \\frac14 \\).  \n\nFirst, \\( P(A \\cap \\neg B) = P(A|\\neg B)P(\\neg B) = \\frac14 \\times \\frac23 = \\frac{1}{6} \\).  \nThen \\( P(A \\cap B) = P(A) - P(A \\cap \\neg B) = \\frac12 - \\frac16 = \\frac13 \\).  \nFinally \\( P(A|B) = \\frac{P(A \\cap B)}{P(B)} = \\frac{\\frac13}{\\frac13} = 1 \\).  \n\nAnswer: \\(\\boxed{D}\\)",
