      "generated_answer": "The score (6, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2) means there are 7 vertices, one of degree 6 and the other six of degree 2.  \nThe degree-6 vertex is connected to all others, so the remaining edges form a 2-regular graph on the 6 vertices of degree 2.  \nA 2-regular graph on 6 labeled vertices is a disjoint union of cycles; the only possibility for all 6 vertices is a single 6-cycle or two 3-cycles.  \n\nNumber of 6-cycles on 6 labeled vertices: \\( \\frac{(6-1)!}{2} = 60/2 = 30 \\) (since cycles are undirected).  \nNumber of ways to split into two 3-cycles: \\( \\frac{1}{2} \\binom{6}{3} \\times \\frac{(3-1)!}{2} \\times \\frac{(3-1)!}{2} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 20 \\times 1 \\times 1 = 10 \\).  \nTotal: \\( 30 + 10 = 40 \\) labeled graphs.  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{G}\n\\]",
