    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "For a large file, the total time per block in version 1 (1,000 bytes) is:  \n25 (seek) + 8 (latency) + 1 (transfer) + (1 + 10) (OS overhead) = 45 msec per 1,000 bytes.  \n\nIn version 2 (4,000 bytes), the time per block is:  \n25 + 8 + 4 (4×1 msec) + (4×1 + 10) = 25+8+4+14 = 51 msec per 4,000 bytes, or 51/4 = 12.75 msec per 1,000 bytes.  \n\nThe ratio (version 2 time / version 1 time) for the same large file is approximately 12.75 / 45 ≈ 0.283, which is close to 1:3.5.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
