    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Of the following, which best approximates the ratio of the number of nonterminal nodes to the total number of nodes in a complete K-ary tree of depth N?\n\nOptions: \nA. N/K\nB. (N-1)/K\nC. K-1/K\nD. N-1/m\nE. log_10 (1/N)\nF. 1/N\nG. (K-1)/N\nH. K/N\nI. 1/(K-1)\nJ. 1/K\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let’s break this down:  \nA complete *K-ary tree of depth N* means depth N has levels 0, 1, …, N.  \nTotal number of nodes = \\(\\frac{K^{N+1} - 1}{K-1}\\).  \nNumber of leaves = \\(K^N\\).  \nNonterminal nodes = total nodes − leaves = \\(\\frac{K^{N+1} - 1}{K-1} - K^N\\).  \n\nRatio of nonterminals to total nodes → simplifies (for large N) approximately to \\(\\frac{K-1}{K}\\) because leaves ≈ \\(K^N\\) out of total ≈ \\(\\frac{K^{N+1}}{K-1}\\), so leaves proportion ≈ \\(\\frac{K-1}{K}\\), nonterminals proportion ≈ \\(1 - \\frac{K-1}{K} = \\frac{1}{K}\\)? Wait — check:  \nLeaves proportion ≈ \\((K-1)/K^{?}\\) → let’s compute ratio directly:\n\nNonterminals/total ≈ \\(\\frac{\\frac{K^{N+1} - 1}{K-1} - K^N}{\\frac{K^{N+1} - 1}{K-1}}\\).  \nMultiply numerator and denominator: For large N, ≈ \\(\\frac{K^{N+1}/(K-1) - K^N}{K^{N+1}/(K-1)} = 1 - \\frac{K-1}{K} = \\frac{1}{K}\\)? Actually:  \n\\( \\frac{K^{N+1}/(K-1) - K^N}{K^{N+1}/(K-1)} = 1 - \\frac{K^N (K-1)}{K^{N+1}} = 1 - \\frac{K-1}{K} = \\frac{1}{K} \\). That’s leaves proportion? No — I swapped: that’s leaves proportion = \\(K-1/K\\). Nonterminals proportion = 1/K.  \n\nBut looking at options, \\( \\frac{K-1}{K} \\) appears as option C, which is the *leaves* proportion, not nonterminals proportion. They ask: nonterminals/total. That’s \\(1/K\\), which is option J.  \n\nFor large N, indeed, nonterminals ≈ \\( (K^{N+1}-1)/(K-1) - K^N\\) → ratio = \\(1 - \\frac{K-1}{K} = 1/K\\).  \n\nSo **J**.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
