    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9408",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A one-hour color video in YUV format has a frame resolution of 1920x1080 with a 4:2:2 color sub-sampling format, 8 bits for each component, and a frame rate of 30 frames/s. Determine the storage requirement for the video in Gbytes (3 sig. fig.).\n\nOptions: \nA. 600\nB. 490\nC. 417\nD. 320\nE. 375\nF. 500\nG. 450\nH. 350\nI. 525\nJ. 275\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, compute bit rate per frame:  \n\n- Luminance (Y): \\(1920 \\times 1080 \\times 8\\) bits  \n- Chrominance (U and V) in 4:2:2: horizontal subsampling 2:1, vertical full.  \n  For each chroma component: \\( \\frac{1920}{2} \\times 1080 \\times 8\\) bits = \\(960 \\times 1080 \\times 8\\) bits.  \n\nSo per component U: \\(960\\times1080\\times8\\) bits, V same.  \n\nTotal bits per frame =  \n\\[\n[1920\\times1080 + 2\\times(960\\times1080)] \\times 8\n\\]\n\\[\n= (1920\\times1080 + 1920\\times1080) \\times 8\n\\]\n\\[\n= (2\\times1920\\times1080) \\times 8 \\ \\text{bits? Wait, check carefully:}\n\\]\n\nActually, YUV 4:2:2 means: Y full 1920×1080, U and V each 960×1080 (horizontal half, vertical full).  \nSo total pixels per frame for all 3 components =  \n\\(1920\\times1080\\) (Y) + \\(960\\times1080\\) (U) + \\(960\\times1080\\) (V)  \n= \\(1920\\times1080 + 1920\\times1080\\)  \n= \\(3840\\times1080\\) pixel-equivalents.  \n\nEach pixel-equivalent is 8 bits (1 byte) per component? No, careful: each Y/U/V sample is 8 bits (1 byte), but they are separate samples. Counting samples:  \nY samples: \\(1920\\times1080\\)  \nU samples: \\(960\\times1080\\)  \nV samples: \\(960\\times1080\\)  \n\nTotal samples per frame = \\(1920\\times1080 + 960\\times1080 + 960\\times1080 = (1920+960+960)\\times1080\\)  \n= \\(3840\\times1080\\) samples.  \n\nEach sample = 1 byte (8 bits).  \nBytes per frame = \\(3840\\times1080\\) bytes.\n\nCheck: 3840×1080 = 4,147,200 bytes per frame.  \n\nAt 30 fps:  \nBytes per second = \\(4,147,200 \\times 30 = 124,416,000\\) B/s.  \n\nFor 1 hour (3600 s):  \nTotal bytes = \\(124,416,000 \\times 3600 = 447,897,600,000\\) bytes.  \n\nConvert to GB (1 GB = \\(10^9\\) bytes):  \n\\(447,897,600,000 / 10^9 \\approx 447.9\\) GB.  \n\nTo 3 sig. fig.: 448 GB. Closest option is 450 GB (G).  \n\n**Final answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{G}\n\\]",
      "success": true,
