  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_computer science_9474",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Consider a 26-key typewriter. Suppose that pushing a key results in printing that letter or the next (with equal probability). Thus A results in A or B, ..., Z results in Z or A. What is the capacity of this channel in bits?\n\nOptions: \nA. 2.0\nB. 2.5\nC. 4.7\nD. 4.5\nE. 1.8\nF. 4.1\nG. 5.0\nH. 3.0\nI. 6.0\nJ. 3.7\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the input \\( X \\in \\{A,\\dots,Z\\} \\) and output \\( Y \\in \\{A,\\dots,Z\\} \\).  \nEach input leads to two equally likely outputs: \\( Y = X \\) or \\( Y = X+1 \\) (mod 26).  \nThis means the channel is symmetric with 26 inputs, each having 2 possible outputs, but outputs can come from 2 possible inputs (except some boundary effects wrap around).  \n\nThe channel matrix is circulant:  \n\\( P(Y=j \\mid X=i) = \\frac12 \\) if \\( j=i \\) or \\( j=i+1 \\pmod{26} \\), else 0.  \n\nFor a symmetric channel, capacity \\( C = \\log_2(26) - H(\\text{row}) \\) where \\( H(\\text{row}) \\) is row entropy.  \nHere each row has 2 nonzero entries probability \\( \\frac12, \\frac12 \\), so \\( H(\\text{row}) = 1 \\) bit.  \n\nThus \\( C = \\log_2(26) - 1 \\approx 4.70044 - 1 = 3.70044 \\) bits, which matches \\( 3.7 \\) bits in the options.  \n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{J}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 184,
        "output_tokens": 267,
        "total_tokens": 451
