      "generated_answer": "The fraction of slots wasted due to multiple simultaneous transmission attempts is the probability that two or more stations transmit in the same slot. This is calculated as 1 minus the probability that no station transmits minus the probability that exactly one station transmits. Using the binomial distribution:  \nP(0) = (1 − 0.35)^5 = 0.65^5 ≈ 0.116,  \nP(1) = 5 × 0.35 × 0.65^4 ≈ 0.312,  \nSo, P(wasted) = 1 − 0.116 − 0.312 = 0.572.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
