      "generated_answer": "A graph has an Euler circuit if and only if every vertex has even degree and the graph is connected. In a complete graph with $ n $ vertices, each vertex has degree $ n-1 $. So, $ K_{12} $ has vertices of degree 11 (odd), so no Euler circuit. $ K_{13} $ has degree 12 (even), so it does have an Euler circuit. A tree with more than 2 vertices has leaves (degree 1), so cannot have an Euler circuit.\n\nThus, only II (the complete graph with 13 vertices) must have an Euler circuit.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
