    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are restricted to using only **AND (∧)** and **OR (∨)** without **NOT (¬)**.  \nWithout negation, we can only represent monotone Boolean functions — conditions that stay true when more variables change from false to true.\n\nI (\"at least three true\") is monotone, so expressible.  \nII (\"exactly three true\") would require excluding the \"all four true\" case, which needs negation.  \nIII (\"even number true\") would require expressing both true counts of 0, 2, 4, but 0 true (all false) cannot be expressed without negation, nor can \"exactly 2 true\" without excluding nearby counts.  \n\nThus only I is expressible.  \n\n\\boxed{G}",
