    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion:  Which of the given formulas of PL is the best symbolization of the following sentence?\nEither England's importing beef is not a necessary condition for France's subsidizing agriculture, or China promotes human rights if South Africa supplies diamonds.\n\nOptions: \nA. (~F ⊃ E) ∨ (C ≡ ~S)\nB. (~E ⊃ F) ∨ (C ⊃ S)\nC. (~F ⊃ E) ∨ (C ≡ S)\nD. ~(F ⊃ E) ∨ (S ⊃ C)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
