      "generated_answer": "First, break down the sentence into logic:  \n\n1. “Either England's importing beef is **not** a necessary condition for France's subsidizing agriculture…”  \n   A necessary condition statement “E is necessary for F” is symbolized as F ⊃ E.  \n   Its negation is ~(F ⊃ E).  \n\n2. “…or China promotes human rights if South Africa supplies diamonds.”  \n   “C if S” means S ⊃ C.  \n\n3. So the whole sentence is: ~(F ⊃ E) ∨ (S ⊃ C).  \n   That matches option **D**.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{D}",
