      "generated_answer": "To solve this problem, we must extract the specific performance percentages for the 2011 program from the provided text and calculate the difference.\n\n**Step-by-step solution:**\n1.  **Identify the maximum percentage:** According to the text regarding the 2011 performance share program, \"participants had the ability to receive up to 150% ( 150 % ) of the target number of shares originally granted.\"\n2.  **Identify the actual percentage:** The text states that for the 2011 program, \"actual performance resulted in participants achieving 130% ( 130 % ) of target.\"\n3.  **Calculate the difference:** To find the difference in percentage points, subtract the actual performance percentage from the maximum percentage: $150 - 130 = 20$.\n\n**Explanation:**\nAccording to the text, the 2011 performance share program allowed participants to receive up to a maximum of 150% of the target number of shares. The actual performance achieved for this program was 130% of the target. The difference in percentage points between the maximum and actual performance is calculated by subtracting 130 from 150, which equals 20.\n\n\\boxed{20}",
