    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_504",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Your company has just written one million units of a one-year European asset-or-nothing put option on an equity index fund. The equity index fund is currently trading at 1000. It pays dividends continuously at a rate proportional to its price; the dividend yield is 2%. It has a volatility of 20%. The option’s payoff will be made only if the equity index fund is down by more than 40% at the end of one year. The continuously compounded risk-free interest rate is 2.5% Using the Black-Scholes model, determine the price of the asset-or-nothing put options. Give the answer in millions.\n\nOptions: \nA. 7.5\nB. 5.2\nC. 3.6\nD. 2.2\nE. 2.5\nF. 4.1\nG. 4.7\nH. 5.9\nI. 1.9\nJ. 6.8\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, identify the parameters:\n\n- \\( S_0 = 1000 \\), \\( K \\) for the “down by more than 40%” condition means \\( S_T < 600 \\) (since \\( 1000 \\times 0.6 = 600 \\)), so the trigger is \\( K = 600 \\).\n- Asset-or-nothing put pays the asset price \\( S_T \\) at expiry if \\( S_T < K \\).\n- Under Black–Scholes, price = \\( S_0 e^{-qT} N(-d_1) \\) for \\( K = 600 \\) (where \\( d_1 = \\frac{\\ln(S_0/K) + (r - q + \\sigma^2/2)T}{\\sigma\\sqrt{T}} \\)).\n\nPlug in: \\( T=1, r=0.025, q=0.02, \\sigma=0.2 \\).\n\nCompute \\( d_1 = \\frac{\\ln(1000/600) + (0.025 - 0.02 + 0.02^2/2)}{0.2} = \\frac{0.510826 + 0.0052}{0.2} \\approx 2.58013 \\) → negative for put? Wait, careful: For asset-or-nothing **put**, we use \\( S_0 e^{-qT} N(-d_1) \\), and \\( d_1 \\) here is large positive because \\( S_0 > K \\) (put is triggered below \\( K \\) which is less than \\( S_0 \\)), so \\( N(-d_1) \\) is small.\n\nActually \\( d_1 = \\frac{\\ln(1000/600) + (0.025 - 0.02 + 0.2^2/2)}{0.2} \\).  \nNumerically:  \n\\( \\ln(1000/600) = 0.510826 \\)  \n\\( r - q + \\sigma^2/2 = 0.025 - 0.02 + 0.02 = 0.025 \\)  \nSum = \\( 0.510826 + 0.025 = 0.535826 \\)  \nDivide by \\( 0.2 \\) → \\( d_1 = 2.67913 \\)  \n\\( N(-d_1) = N(-2.679) \\) ≈ \\( 0.003699 \\) (very small).  \n\nPrice per unit = \\( 1000 e^{-0.02} \\times 0.003699 \\approx 980.2 \\times 0.003699 \\approx 3.625 \\) per unit.\n\nOne million units → total ≈ 3.625 million.\n\nMatches option **C: 3.6**.\n\n**Correct choice: C**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{C}\n\\]",
