  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_433",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: assume you are Indonesian. In 2010, the rupiah exchange rate was around IDR15,000/USD, and the consumer price index in Indonesia and the United States was at 100. In 2019, the exchange rate changed to IDR14,000/USD. Simultaneously, Indonesia’s inflation rose 5% due to the consumer price index rising to 105. Meanwhile, the United States’ inflation rate rose 10% due to the consumer price index rising to 110. Whats the real exchange rate?\n\nOptions: \nA. 14000.00\nB. 15500.00\nC. 15000.00\nD. 16000.00\nE. 13500.00\nF. 14666.67\nG. 13888.89\nH. 14800.00\nI. 15200.00\nJ. 13333.33\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We can use the real exchange rate formula:  \n\n\\[\n\\text{Real exchange rate} = \\text{Nominal exchange rate} \\times \\frac{P_{\\text{foreign}}}{P_{\\text{domestic}}}\n\\]  \n\nHere, \\(P_{\\text{foreign}}\\) is US CPI, \\(P_{\\text{domestic}}\\) is Indonesia CPI, and the nominal rate is expressed as IDR/USD.  \n\n2019 nominal rate = \\(14000\\)  \n\\(P_{\\text{US}} = 110\\), \\(P_{\\text{ID}} = 105\\)  \n\n\\[\n\\text{Real exchange rate} = 14000 \\times \\frac{110}{105} \\approx 14666.67\n\\]  \n\nThat matches option F.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
