  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_business_51",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Assume the following model (from the preceding problem). Y = C + I + G C = 100 + 0.6Y I = 0.2Y - 50i M_D = 0.25Y - 30i M_s = 65 G = 100 whose equilibrium level was found to be 500. Suppose that full employment level of income is 600, so that the desired change is 100. If the money supply is held constant, what change in govern-ment spending will be required to close the deflationary gap?\n\nOptions: \nA. 80\nB. 75\nC. 55\nD. 90\nE. 50\nF. 61.5\nG. 70\nH. 85\nI. 100\nJ. 65\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We need to find the change in government spending \\(\\Delta G\\) to raise \\(Y\\) by 100 when money supply is fixed.  \n\nFrom the goods market equilibrium \\(Y = C + I + G\\):  \n\\(C = 100 + 0.6Y\\)  \n\\(I = 0.2Y - 50i\\)  \nSo \\(Y = 100 + 0.6Y + 0.2Y - 50i + G\\)  \n\\(Y - 0.8Y = 100 - 50i + G\\)  \n\\(0.2Y = 100 - 50i + G\\)  (1)  \n\nFrom the money market equilibrium \\(M_s = M_D\\):  \n\\(65 = 0.25Y - 30i \\Rightarrow i = \\frac{0.25Y - 65}{30}\\)  (2)  \n\nSubstituting (2) into (1) to eliminate \\(i\\) and solving for \\(Y\\) as a function of \\(G\\) would give the multiplier under constant \\(M_s\\).  \n\nDoing this (or using known IS-LM formulas for slope), the fiscal multiplier under fixed \\(M_s\\) here is \\(\\frac{\\Delta Y}{\\Delta G} = \\frac{1}{1-0.8 + \\frac{50}{30} \\times 0.25}\\).  \nFirst term: \\(1-0.8=0.2\\). The extra term: \\(\\frac{50}{30}\\times 0.25 = \\frac{12.5}{30} = 0.416\\bar{6}\\).  \n\nThus denominator \\(= 0.2 + 0.416\\bar{6} = 0.616\\bar{6}\\).  \n\nMultiplier \\(= 1 / 0.616\\bar{6} \\approx 1.6216\\).  \n\nSo \\(\\Delta G = \\Delta Y / 1.6216 \\approx 100 / 1.6216 \\approx 61.68\\), which matches option **F: 61.5** (rounding difference).  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{F}\n\\]",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
