    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To estimate the final inventory, first calculate the cost of goods sold (COGS). With an 18% margin on sales, the cost of goods sold is 82% of $3,485 = 0.82 × 3,485 = $2,857.70. Then, use the inventory formula: Ending Inventory = Beginning Inventory + Purchases − COGS = $2,300 + $1,125 − $2,857.70 = $567.30.\n\nThus, the correct answer is \\boxed{B}.",
