    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The rental is for 2 days and 4 hours, which exceeds two 24-hour periods, so the minimum charge is 3 daily rates (since any part of a day counts as a full day or hour over, and the minimum charge is a 24-hour rate). Thus, 3 days × $12.00 = $36.00 for rental. The extra 4 hours are charged at $2.75/hour: 4 × $2.75 = $11.00. Mileage cost is 364 miles × $0.14 = $50.96. Insurance is $1.20 (collision) + $1.20 (liability) = $2.40 per day; for 3 days: 3 × $2.40 = $7.20. Total: $36.00 + $11.00 + $50.96 + $7.20 = $105.16. However, since the 2-day rate may be intended, but 2 days + 4 hours triggers a third day charge, yet possibly only two full days plus 4 hours at hourly rate. Rechecking: 2 days = $24.00, 4 hours = 4 × $2.75 = $11.00, mileage $50.96, insurance: 3 days? But even 2 days with extra hours = 3 units → insurance $2.40 × 3 = $7.20 → total $24 + $11 + $50.96 + $7.20 = $93.16.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
