    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Without additional context or specific premium tables, it's impossible to determine the exact cost from the options. However, based on typical life insurance pricing, an endowment policy (which pays the face amount whether the insured lives or dies) is significantly more expensive than a limited payment policy (which pays only upon death but has premium payments limited to a shorter period). The option that seems most plausibly high for an endowment policy premium at age 45 is **$233.35**.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{C}",
