    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6319",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following estimation techniques are available for the estimation of over-identified systems of simultaneous equations?\n\ni) OLS\n\nii) ILS\n\niii) 2SLS\n\niv) IV\n\nOptions: \nA. (iii) only\nB. (i), (iii) and (iv) only\nC. (ii), (iii), and (iv) only\nD. (i), (ii) and (iii) only\nE. (i) and (iii) only\nF. (ii) and (iv) only\nG. (i) and (ii) only\nH. (i), (ii), (iii) and (iv)\nI. (i), (ii) and (iv) only\nJ. (iii) and (iv) only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "For over-identified systems of simultaneous equations, Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) is inconsistent due to simultaneity bias, so (i) is incorrect. Indirect Least Squares (ILS) can be used only for exactly identified equations, not over-identified ones, so (ii) is not suitable. The appropriate methods are Two-Stage Least Squares (2SLS) and Instrumental Variables (IV), both of which are valid for over-identified systems.\n\nThus, the correct answer is **J**.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
