      "generated_answer": "The fixed cost does not change with output, so the marginal fixed cost (MFC) is zero.  \nMarginal variable cost (MVC) is the change in variable cost from producing one more unit, and marginal total cost (MC) is the change in total cost, which equals MFC + MVC = 0 + MVC.  \nTherefore, MFC = 0 and MVC = MC.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
