      "generated_answer": "To forecast 10-day volatility using a GARCH model, the correct approach is to generate the 10-step ahead conditional variance forecast, which accounts for the predicted variance at horizon 10, and then take its square root to obtain the standard deviation. This reflects the expected volatility over the 10-day horizon based on the GARCH model dynamics. Other options incorrectly combine multiple forecasts or scale the one-step forecast inappropriately.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
