    "global index": "MMLUPro_economics_6325",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Miss Lane had the following income tax information in 1978 while she worked as a reporter on a large metropolitan news paper: Taxable income $15,000 Exemptions 1,500 Business Expenses 6,000 Non business Expenses 3,000 Find Miss Lane's adjusted gross income and gross income for 1978.\n\nOptions: \nA. Adjusted Gross Income: $19,500, Gross Income: $25,500\nB. Adjusted Gross Income: $8,500, Gross Income: $23,500\nC. Adjusted Gross Income: $20,000, Gross Income: $25,000\nD. Adjusted Gross Income: $9,000, Gross Income: $21,000\nE. Adjusted Gross Income: $16,500, Gross Income: $28,500\nF. Adjusted Gross Income: $12,000, Gross Income: $27,000\nG. Adjusted Gross Income: $11,500, Gross Income: $22,500\nH. Adjusted Gross Income: $10,500, Gross Income: $20,500\nI. Adjusted Gross Income: $19,000, Gross Income: $26,000\nJ. Adjusted Gross Income: $18,500, Gross Income: $24,500\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find Miss Lane's gross income, add her taxable income ($15,000), exemptions ($1,500), and deductions (business expenses $6,000 and non-business expenses $3,000 are typically subtracted after gross income, not added). However, gross income is generally higher than taxable income before deductions. Adjusted Gross Income (AGI) is calculated as gross income minus adjustments like business expenses. Working backwards: if taxable income is $15,000, and exemptions and deductions are subtracted after AGI, AGI = taxable income + exemptions + non-business deductions = $15,000 + $1,500 + $3,000 = $19,500? But business expenses reduce gross income to get AGI. Correct logic: Gross Income = AGI + Business Expenses = $19,500 + $6,000 = $25,500. Thus, AGI = $19,500 and Gross Income = $25,500 fits.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
