      "generated_answer": "Interest payments on government bonds are not included in national income because they do not reflect current production or income generation; instead, they are considered transfer payments that redistribute income from taxpayers to bondholders. Unlike interest from private firms, which results from productive investment and contributes to current output, government interest payments are financed by taxation or borrowing and do not directly generate goods or services. Therefore, they are excluded from national income calculations.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
