      "generated_answer": "Plausible approaches to dealing with heteroscedasticity include using suitably modified standard errors (such as robust standard errors), applying generalized least squares (GLS) to account for the variance structure, and sometimes transforming variables (e.g., logarithms) to stabilize variance. Adding lagged values does not directly address heteroscedasticity and is more relevant for autocorrelation. Therefore, the correct approaches are (i), (ii), and (iii).\n\n\\boxed{J}",
