      "generated_answer": "The free rider problem occurs when individuals benefit from public goods without contributing to their cost, leading to under-provision. The government can most effectively address this by supplying public goods using tax dollars, ensuring universal access and funding through compulsory taxation. This approach prevents exclusion and ensures provision despite non-excludability.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
