      "generated_answer": "In a jurisdiction following common law riparian rights rather than prior appropriation, priority is not based solely on the timing of use, which disqualifies options relying on the \"first in time\" principle. In times of water scarcity, common law courts often accord priority to domestic and residential needs over agricultural or commercial irrigation needs due to the essential nature of the use. Therefore, the rancher's domestic claim would be protected against the millionaire's agricultural use.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
