tly states that the income is to be paid to the living children of Harriet only after the death of Stan's widow.\nI. No, because the Rule against Perpetuities prevents the trust from being held indefinitely.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
