esearchers. The professors expect to make their study available through a Web site, www.eeo1.com. The Blumrosens, who were instrumental in setting up the E.E.O.C. in 1965, also say the government should make more active use of their data. The commission said it did not comment on draft reports. \nQuestion: In what way can one determine what companies are being discriminatory?\n\nProvided Answer: \n\n Is the provided answer correct? Provide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct choice. ",
