      "generated_answer": "We have \\(\\log_x(y^x) = \\frac{x \\ln y}{\\ln x} = 10\\).  \n\nAlso \\(\\log_y(x^{4y}) = \\frac{4y \\ln x}{\\ln y} = 10\\).\n\nLet \\(a = \\ln x\\), \\(b = \\ln y\\). Then the system is:  \n\n\\[\n\\frac{x b}{a} = 10 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x b = 10 a\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{4y a}{b} = 10 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad 4y a = 10 b\n\\]\n\nAlso \\(x = e^a\\), \\(y = e^b\\). Multiply the two equations: \\((x b)(4y a) = (10a)(10b)\\)  \n\\(\\Rightarrow 4xy ab = 100 ab\\).  \n\nSince \\(a,b \\neq 0\\) and \\(x,y>1\\), \\(ab \\neq 0\\), cancel \\(ab\\): \\(4xy = 100 \\Rightarrow xy = 25\\).\n\nFinal: \\(\\boxed{25}\\).",
