    "global index": "AIME_79",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let $\\omega\\neq 1$ be a 13th root of unity. Find the remainder when\n\\[\\prod_{{k=0}}^{{12}}(2-2\\omega^k+\\omega^{{2k}})\\]\nis divided by 1000.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The product is \\(\\prod_{k=0}^{12} (2 - 2\\omega^k + \\omega^{2k})\\) with \\(\\omega = e^{2\\pi i/13}\\).  \nRewrite as \\(\\prod_{k=0}^{12} (1 + (1 - \\omega^k)^2)\\), and substitute \\(x = 1 - \\omega^k\\) noting \\(\\prod_{k=0}^{12} (x - (1-\\omega^k)) = x^{13} - 1\\) after change of variable.  \nThen \\(\\prod_{k=0}^{12} (1 + x_k^2) = \\prod_{k=0}^{12} (i - x_k)(-i - x_k) = [(i)^{13} - 1][(-i)^{13} - 1] = (i^{13} - 1)((-i)^{13} - 1)\\).\n\nNow \\(i^{13} = i^{12} \\cdot i = 1\\cdot i = i\\), so product = \\((i - 1)(-i - 1) = -(i - 1)(i + 1) = - (i^2 - 1) = -(-1 - 1) = 2\\).  \nRemainder when \\(2\\) is divided by \\(1000\\) is \\(2\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
