      "generated_answer": "Let \\( z = 4e^{i\\theta} \\). Then \\( \\frac{1}{z} = \\frac{1}{4} e^{-i\\theta} \\).  \n\nThe expression is  \n\\[\n(75+117i) \\cdot 4e^{i\\theta} + (96+144i) \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} e^{-i\\theta}.\n\\]  \nSimplify:  \n\\[\n= (300+468i) e^{i\\theta} + (24+36i) e^{-i\\theta}.\n\\]  \n\nWrite \\( e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta \\). Let \\( A = 300 + 468i \\), \\( B = 24 + 36i \\).  \nWe have \\( A e^{i\\theta} + B e^{-i\\theta} = (A+B)\\cos\\theta + i(A-B)\\sin\\theta \\) after using \\( e^{\\pm i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta \\pm i\\sin\\theta \\) carefully.  \n\nActually compute more directly:  \nLet \\( w = e^{i\\theta} \\). Expression: \\( Aw + B \\overline{w} \\) since \\( e^{-i\\theta} = \\overline{w} \\) when \\( |w| = 1 \\).  \n\nReal part: Re\\([Aw + B\\overline{w}]\\) = Re\\([(A+B)\\cos\\theta + i(A-B)\\sin\\theta]\\). Let \\( C = A+B = 324 + 504i \\) and \\( D = A-B = 276 + 432i \\).  \n\nReal part = Re\\([C\\cos\\theta + iD\\sin\\theta]\\) = \\( 324\\cos\\theta - 432\\sin\\theta \\).  \n\nSo Re = \\( 324\\cos\\theta - 432\\sin\\theta \\).  \nMaximum of \\( R\\cos\\theta - S\\sin\\theta \\) is \\( \\sqrt{R^2 + S^2} \\) with \\( R=324, S=432 \\).  \n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{324^2 + 432^2} = \\sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \\sqrt{291600} = 540.\n\\]  \n\nThus the largest possible real part is \\( 540 \\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{540}\n\\]",
