    "global index": "AsDiv_1425",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A boat goes 30 km upstream and 44 km downstream in 10 hours. In 13 hours, it can go 40 km upstream and 55 km downstream.\n\nQuestion: Determine the speed of the stream and that of boat in still water.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let \\( u \\) be the speed of the boat in still water (km/h) and \\( v \\) be the speed of the stream (km/h).  \nUpstream speed = \\( u - v \\), downstream speed = \\( u + v \\).  \n\nFrom the problem:  \n\\[\n\\frac{30}{u-v} + \\frac{44}{u+v} = 10\n\\]  \n\\[\n\\frac{40}{u-v} + \\frac{55}{u+v} = 13\n\\]  \n\nLet \\( a = \\frac{1}{u-v} \\), \\( b = \\frac{1}{u+v} \\).  \n\\[\n30a + 44b = 10 \\quad (1)\n\\]  \n\\[\n40a + 55b = 13 \\quad (2)\n\\]  \n\nMultiply (1) by 4 and (2) by 3:  \n\\[\n120a + 176b = 40\n\\]  \n\\[\n120a + 165b = 39\n\\]  \nSubtract: \\( 11b = 1 \\Rightarrow b = \\frac{1}{11} \\)  \n\nFrom (1): \\( 30a + 4 = 10 \\Rightarrow 30a = 6 \\Rightarrow a = \\frac{1}{5} \\)  \n\nThus:  \n\\[\nu - v = 5, \\quad u + v = 11\n\\]  \nAdding: \\( 2u = 16 \\Rightarrow u = 8 \\)  \nSubtracting: \\( 2v = 6 \\Rightarrow v = 3 \\)  \n\n**Final answer**:  \n\\[\n\\boxed{{8 \\text{ km/h}, 3 \\text{ km/h}}}\n\\]",
