    "global index": "AsDiv_1433",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A man walks certain distance with certain speed. If he walks 1/2 km/hr faster, he takes 1 hr less. But if he walks 1 km/hr slower, he takes 3 more hours.\n\nQuestion: Find the distance covered by the man and his original rate of walking.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "deepseek/deepseek-v3.2",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let \\( d \\) be the distance (in km) and \\( r \\) be his original speed (in km/hr).  \nTime originally: \\( t = \\frac{d}{r} \\).  \n\nFirst condition: walking \\(\\frac12\\) km/hr faster, time is 1 hr less:  \n\\[\n\\frac{d}{r+\\frac12} = \\frac{d}{r} - 1.\n\\]  \n\nSecond condition: walking 1 km/hr slower, time is 3 hr more:  \n\\[\n\\frac{d}{r-1} = \\frac{d}{r} + 3.\n\\]  \n\nFrom the first equation:  \n\\[\n\\frac{d}{r+\\frac12} = \\frac{d}{r} - 1\n\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\nd\\left[ \\frac{1}{r} - \\frac{1}{r+\\frac12} \\right] = 1.\n\\]  \nThe bracket simplifies to \\(\\frac{r+\\frac12 - r}{r(r+\\frac12)} = \\frac{1/2}{r(r+\\frac12)}\\), so:  \n\\[\n\\frac{d}{2r(r+\\frac12)} = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad d = 2r\\left(r+\\frac12\\right). \\quad (1)\n\\]  \n\nFrom the second equation:  \n\\[\n\\frac{d}{r-1} - \\frac{d}{r} = 3\n\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\nd\\left[ \\frac{1}{r-1} - \\frac{1}{r} \\right] = 3.\n\\]  \nThe bracket simplifies to \\(\\frac{r - (r-1)}{r(r-1)} = \\frac{1}{r(r-1)}\\), so:  \n\\[\n\\frac{d}{r(r-1)} = 3 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad d = 3r(r-1). \\quad (2)\n\\]  \n\nEquate (1) and (2):  \n\\[\n2r\\left(r+\\frac12\\right) = 3r(r-1).\n\\]  \n\\[\n2r^2 + r = 3r^2 - 3r\n\\Rightarrow 0 = r^2 - 4r\n\\Rightarrow r(r-4) = 0.\n\\]  \n\\( r = 0 \\) invalid, so \\( r = 4 \\) km/hr.  \n\nFrom (2): \\( d = 3 \\times 4 \\times 3 = 36 \\) km.  \n\n**Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{{4, 36}}\n\\]  \n(Speed \\( 4 \\) km/hr, distance \\( 36 \\) km.)",
