    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the fraction be $\\frac{x}{y}$. According to the problem:  \n1) $\\frac{x+1}{y+1} = \\frac{4}{5}$ → $5(x+1) = 4(y+1)$ → $5x + 5 = 4y + 4$ → $5x - 4y = -1$  \n2) $\\frac{x-5}{y-5} = \\frac{1}{2}$ → $2(x-5) = 1(y-5)$ → $2x - 10 = y - 5$ → $2x - y = 5$  \n\nSolving the system: from equation (2), $y = 2x - 5$. Substitute into (1):  \n$5x - 4(2x - 5) = -1$ → $5x - 8x + 20 = -1$ → $-3x = -21$ → $x = 7$, then $y = 2(7) - 5 = 9$.  \n\nThus, the original fraction is $\\boxed{\\frac{7}{9}}$.",
