      "generated_answer": "We determine the components of $\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\end{pmatrix}$ by setting up a system of linear equations based on the given conditions. The dot product $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{v} = 2$ implies $x + y + z = 2$, while the cross product $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$ yields the equations $z - y = 1$ and $x - z = -2$. Solving these for $x$ and $y$ gives $x = z - 2$ and $y = z - 1$, and substituting these into the dot product equation results in $3z - 3 = 2$, from which $z = 5/3$, $x = -1/3$, and $y = 2/3$.\n\nFinal Answer:\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3} \\end{pmatrix}}",
