      "generated_answer": "The transformation \\(F(z)\\) is a Möbius map with fixed points at \\(\\pm i\\).  \nBy induction, \\(z_n = F^{\\circ n}(z_0)\\) has the general form  \n\\[\nz_n = \\frac{(z_0+i)e^{2ni\\theta} + (z_0-i)}{(z_0+i)e^{2ni\\theta} - (z_0-i)}\n\\]\nwhere \\(e^{i\\theta} = \\frac{z_0+i}{z_0-i}\\).  \n\nDirect computation gives \\(z_0+i = \\frac1{137}+2i\\) and \\(z_0-i = \\frac1{137}\\).  \nSince \\(|(z_0+i)/(z_0-i)| = |1+2i\\cdot137|/\\sqrt{1+137^2} = |1+274i|/\\sqrt{1+137^2} = \\sqrt{1+274^2}/\\sqrt{1+137^2} >1\\),  \nthe sequence converges to the repelling fixed point \\(i\\), but for exact \\(n=2002\\):  \n\nLet \\(w_0 = \\frac{z_0+i}{z_0-i} = 1+274i\\), so \\(|w_0| = \\sqrt{1+274^2}\\).  \nThen \\(w_n = w_0^{2^n}\\) for even iteration? Actually: \\(F(z)=\\frac{z+i}{z-i}\\) has multiplier \\(-1\\) for the fixed point \\(i\\) if linearized, but here let's check directly:  \nRewrite \\(z_n = \\frac{z_{n-1}+i}{z_{n-1}-i}\\). Let \\(t_n = \\frac{z_n-i}{z_n+i}\\), then \\(t_{n} = -\\, t_{n-1}\\). So \\(t_n = (-1)^n t_0\\).  \nNow \\(t_0 = \\frac{z_0-i}{z_0+i} = \\frac{1/137}{1/137 + 2i} = \\frac{1}{1+274i}\\).  \nThus \\(t_{2002} = (-1)^{2002} t_0 = t_0\\).  \nSo \\(z_{2002}-i = t_0(z_{2002}+i) \\implies z_{2002} = \\frac{i(1+t_0)}{1-t_0}\\).  \n\nCompute \\(1+t_0 = 1 + \\frac{1}{1+274i} = \\frac{1+274i+1}{1+274i} = \\frac{2+274i}{1+274i}\\).  \n\\(1-t_0 = 1 - \\frac{1}{1+274i} = \\frac{1+274i-1}{1+274i} = \\frac{274i}{1+274i}\\).  \nThus \\(z_{2002} = i\\cdot\\frac{2+274i}{274i} = i\\cdot\\frac{2+274i}{274i} = \\frac{i(2+274i)}{274i} = \\frac{2i-274}{274i}\\)? Wait, carefully:  \n\n\\(z_{2002} = i\\cdot\\frac{1+t_0}{1-t_0} = i\\cdot\\frac{\\frac{2+274i}{1+274i}}{\\frac{274i}{1+274i}} = i\\cdot\\frac{2+274i}{274i} = \\frac{2+274i}{274} = \\frac{1}{137} + i\\).  \n\nHence \\(z_{2002} = z_0\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{137}+i}\n\\]",
